msgid "The Free Bible"
msgstr "Die Vrye Bybel"

msgid ""
"While Bibledit may be used for making any Bibles, there are some distinct "
"advantages to releasing Bibles under a free license."
msgstr ""
"Hoewel Bibledit gebruik kan word om enige Bybels te maak, is daar sekere "
"duidelike voordele daaraan verbonde om Bybels onder 'n vrye lisensie vry te "
"stel."

msgid ""
"Others will feel free to publish the open Bible. You don't need to do "
"everything yourself: Others will help spreading the Word of God."
msgstr ""
"Ander sal vry voel om die oop Bybel te publiseer. U hoef nie alles self te "
"doen nie: Ander sal help om die Woord van God te versprei."

msgid ""
"It becomes easy to publish Bibles in a variety of formats by a variety of "
"people: on paper, phones, the Internet."
msgstr ""
"Dit word maklik om Bybels in 'n verskeidenheid formate deur 'n "
"verskeidenheid mense te publiseer: op papier, foon, die Internet."

msgid ""
"If you think that the Bible you translated is good and reliable, and you "
"release it under an open license, it will rapidly spread over the Internet."
msgstr ""
"As u dink dat die Bybel wat u vertaal het goed en betroubaar is, en u stel "
"dit onder 'n oop lisensie vry, sal dit vinnig oor die Internet versprei."

msgid ""
"Compare an open Bible to the Greek minuscules: They were copied freely, and "
"they can now be found all over the place."
msgstr ""
"Vergelyk 'n oop Bybel met die Griekse minuskels: Hulle is vrylik gekopieer, "
"en hulle kan nou orals gevind word."

msgid "Freely you received, freely give."
msgstr "Vrylik het u ontvang, gee vrylik."

msgid ""
"Various church people regularly express a desire to have a more accurate "
"Bible than what they have now."
msgstr ""
"Verskeie kerkmense spreek gereeld 'n begeerte uit om 'n akkurater Bybel te "
"hê as wat hulle nou het."

msgid "The years pass by and the desire becomes stronger."
msgstr "Die jare gaan verby en die begeerte word sterker."

msgid ""
"They pray about the matter, discuss it, and decide to start the work on "
"improving the Bible themselves, with the help of a booklet with directions."
msgstr ""
"Hulle bid oor die saak, bespreek dit, en besluit om self met die werk aan "
"die verbetering van die Bybel te begin, met die hulp van 'n boekie met "
"aanwysings."

msgid "The booklet is published by the Bible Society."
msgstr "Die boekie word deur die Bybelgenootskap gepubliseer."

msgid "Over the years some people join the group, and others leave the group."
msgstr ""
"Oor die jare sluit sommige mense by die groep aan, en ander verlaat die "
"groep."

msgid ""
"The church now has a translation team consisting of four people who by the "
"grace of God work full time on the revision of the Bible."
msgstr ""
"Die kerk het nou 'n vertaalspan bestaande uit vier mense wat deur die genade"
" van God voltyds aan die hersiening van die Bybel werk."

msgid "Each of the four people bring in their own expertise."
msgstr "Elkeen van die vier mense bring hul eie kundigheid in."

msgid "Two of them focus on the target language."
msgstr "Twee van hulle fokus op die teikentaal."

msgid ""
"They aim at using accurate, faithful, beautiful and contemporary language."
msgstr ""
"Hulle mik daarna om akkurate, getroue, mooi en eietydse taal te gebruik."

msgid "One of them focuses on the original Greek and Hebrew."
msgstr "Een van hulle fokus op die oorspronklike Grieks en Hebreeus."

msgid "He ensures that the translated text matches the originals."
msgstr "Hy sorg dat die vertaalde teks met die oorspronklikes ooreenstem."

msgid "One of them focuses, more than the others, on the recipients."
msgstr "Een van hulle fokus, meer as die ander, op die ontvangers."

msgid "She aims at acceptance of the language by the future readers."
msgstr ""
"Sy mik daarna om aanvaarding van die taal deur die toekomstige lesers te "
"verkry."

msgid "Many proof-readers contribute to the work."
msgstr "Baie proeflesers dra tot die werk by."

msgid ""
"The translation team regularly consults with language scholars and church "
"representatives about the Bible translation."
msgstr ""
"Die vertaalspan raadpleeg gereeld taalkundiges en kerkverteenwoordigers oor "
"die Bybelvertaling."

msgid ""
"The Bible Society answers queries about how to translate difficult passages."
msgstr ""
"Die Bybelgenootskap beantwoord navrae oor hoe om moeilike gedeeltes te "
"vertaal."

msgid "After several years the New Testament becomes ready."
msgstr "Na verskeie jare word die Nuwe Testament gereed."

msgid "The manuscript is submitted to the Bible Society for publishing."
msgstr "Die manuskrip word aan die Bybelgenootskap voorgelê vir publisering."

msgid "The manuscript is formatted and uploaded to the church website."
msgstr "Die manuskrip word geformateer en op die kerk se webwerf opgelaai."

msgid ""
"It can now be used by whoever wants to do so before it would be published in"
" paper form."
msgstr ""
"Dit kan nou gebruik word deur wie ook al dit wil doen voordat dit in "
"papiervorm gepubliseer sou word."

msgid "The translation team starts to translate the Old Testament."
msgstr "Die vertaalspan begin die Ou Testament vertaal."

msgid "The years pass by."
msgstr "Die jare gaan verby."

msgid ""
"The team eagerly awaits news from the Bible Society about publishing the New"
" Testament."
msgstr ""
"Die span wag gretig op nuus van die Bybelgenootskap oor die publisering van "
"die Nuwe Testament."

msgid ""
"Five years later the news arrives that the Bible Society starts the "
"preparations for publishing it."
msgstr ""
"Vyf jaar later kom die nuus dat die Bybelgenootskap die voorbereidings vir "
"publisering begin."

msgid ""
"Another year later the team sees the first copies of the New Testament in "
"book form."
msgstr ""
"Nog 'n jaar later sien die span die eerste eksemplare van die Nuwe Testament"
" in boekvorm."

msgid ""
"During all those years the New Testament has been locked up in the offices "
"of the Bible Society."
msgstr ""
"Gedurende al daardie jare was die Nuwe Testament in die kantore van die "
"Bybelgenootskap toegesluit."

msgid ""
"It was not free to go out to the people in book form, but was kept locked "
"up."
msgstr ""
"Dit was nie vry om in boekvorm na die mense uit te gaan nie, maar is "
"toegesluit gehou."

msgid "It was enslaved."
msgstr "Dit was verslaaf."

msgid "The team keeps working on the Old Testament during many years."
msgstr "Die span werk baie jare lank aan die Ou Testament voort."

msgid "They are enabled to do so by the Lord God."
msgstr "Hulle word deur die Here God in staat gestel om dit te doen."

msgid "The Old Testament becomes ready."
msgstr "Die Ou Testament word gereed."

msgid ""
"The manuscript of the whole Bible is submitted to the Bible Society for "
"publishing."
msgstr ""
"Die manuskrip van die hele Bybel word aan die Bybelgenootskap voorgelê vir "
"publisering."

msgid ""
"One member of the translation team suggests to upload the formatted "
"manuscript to the church website, just as was done with the New Testament."
msgstr ""
"Een lid van die vertaalspan stel voor om die geformateerde manuskrip op die "
"kerk se webwerf op te laai, net soos met die Nuwe Testament gedoen is."

msgid ""
"The team leader decides to not do this, but let the Bible Society be the "
"first to publish the Bible."
msgstr ""
"Die spanleier besluit om dit nie te doen nie, maar laat die Bybelgenootskap "
"die eerste wees om die Bybel te publiseer."

msgid ""
"The translator feels disappointed, because the Bible, now complete and "
"accurate, is not free to go out to the people."
msgstr ""
"Die vertaler voel teleurgesteld, omdat die Bybel, nou volledig en akkuraat, "
"nie vry is om na die mense uit te gaan nie."

msgid "Not in paper form, not in digital form."
msgstr "Nie in papiervorm nie, nie in digitale vorm nie."

msgid "It is enslaved, again."
msgstr "Dit is verslaaf, weer."

msgid ""
"Over the years the translator heard stories from others who had similar "
"experiences."
msgstr ""
"Oor die jare het die vertaler stories gehoor van ander wat soortgelyke "
"ervarings gehad het."

msgid "It occurs to him that the current way of doing things is not right."
msgstr "Dit tref hom dat die huidige manier van doen nie reg is nie."

msgid ""
"It leads to a situation where the Bible is not free to go where it is needed"
" most:"
msgstr ""
"Dit lei tot 'n situasie waar die Bybel nie vry is om te gaan waar dit die "
"meeste nodig is nie:"

msgid "To the people."
msgstr "Na die mense."

msgid ""
"The translator begins to see more clearly that Christians should have "
"freedom to publish Bibles or portions of it any time they wish to do so."
msgstr ""
"Die vertaler begin duideliker insien dat Christene vryheid moet hê om Bybels"
" of dele daarvan te publiseer wanneer hulle ook al wil."

msgid "The translator becomes the leader of the translation team."
msgstr "Die vertaler word die leier van die vertaalspan."

msgid "The team leader is acquainted with open licenses."
msgstr "Die spanleier is vertroud met oop lisensies."

msgid ""
"He chooses the GNU Free Documentation License as an appropriate license for "
"the Bible."
msgstr ""
"Hy kies die GNU Free Documentation License as 'n gepaste lisensie vir die "
"Bybel."

msgid ""
"He is of the view that it is appropriate for the Word of God to be created "
"under an open license to allow it to have free course."
msgstr ""
"Hy is van mening dat dit gepas is dat die Woord van God onder 'n oop "
"lisensie geskep word sodat dit vrye loop kan hê."

msgid ""
"The GNU Free Documentation License allows noncommercial distribution of the "
"Bible by anyone who accepts the license."
msgstr ""
"Die GNU Free Documentation License laat nie-kommersiële verspreiding van die"
" Bybel toe deur enigiemand wat die lisensie aanvaar."

msgid ""
"That is a good thing because this enables anyone to print the Bible and give"
" it to someone else."
msgstr ""
"Dit is 'n goeie ding, want dit stel enigiemand in staat om die Bybel te druk"
" en aan iemand anders te gee."

msgid ""
"The GNU Free Documentation License allows commercial distribution of the "
"Bible by any publisher who accepts the license."
msgstr ""
"Die GNU Free Documentation License laat kommersiële verspreiding van die "
"Bybel toe deur enige uitgewer wat die lisensie aanvaar."

msgid ""
"This is good, because it maximizes the distribution potential by allowing "
"sales of printed Bibles."
msgstr ""
"Dit is goed, want dit maksimeer die verspreidingspotensiaal deur die verkoop"
" van gedrukte Bybels toe te laat."

msgid "It also harnesses the profit motive for distribution."
msgstr "Dit span ook die winsmotief vir verspreiding in."

msgid "It limits overcharging with competitive pressure on prices."
msgstr "Dit beperk oorberekening deur mededingende druk op pryse."

msgid ""
"The GNU Free Documentation License allows to update the Bible, provided the "
"updated version is shared under the same license."
msgstr ""
"Die GNU Free Documentation License laat toe dat die Bybel opgedateer word, "
"mits die opgedateerde weergawe onder dieselfde lisensie gedeel word."

msgid ""
"This is a good thing because it allows legitimate updates, revisions, "
"adaptations with no hassle to the translators and no delay for getting "
"permission."
msgstr ""
"Dit is 'n goeie ding, want dit laat wettige opdaterings, hersienings, "
"aanpassings toe sonder gesukkel vir die vertalers en sonder vertraging om "
"toestemming te kry."

msgid ""
"A disadvantage is that changes can be made by people who might not be "
"qualified or called to make changes, with possibly heretical results."
msgstr ""
"'n Nadeel is dat veranderinge deur mense gemaak kan word wat nie "
"gekwalifiseer of geroep is om veranderinge te maak nie, met moontlik "
"ketterse resultate."

msgid ""
"There is some fear that granting permission to make revisions would make it "
"easier for somebody to make heretical changes to the Bible."
msgstr ""
"Daar is 'n mate van vrees dat die verlening van toestemming om hersienings "
"te maak dit vir iemand makliker sal maak om ketterse veranderinge aan die "
"Bybel aan te bring."

msgid "But copyright law is not about preventing this."
msgstr "Maar outeursreg gaan nie daaroor om dit te verhoed nie."

msgid "If anyone wants to make those changes, he would still do it."
msgstr "As iemand daardie veranderinge wil maak, sal hy dit steeds doen."

msgid ""
"There is no need for this fear, because it is God who protects His own work."
msgstr ""
"Daar is geen nodigheid vir hierdie vrees nie, want dit is God wat Sy eie "
"werk beskerm."

msgid "He makes clear what is a good translation, and what is not."
msgstr "Hy maak duidelik wat 'n goeie vertaling is, en wat nie."

msgid ""
"If a Bible Society is so protective about a Bible, so as not to grant a "
"license to make revisions, then there is a bigger danger than that of "
"heresy."
msgstr ""
"As 'n Bybelgenootskap so beskermend is oor 'n Bybel dat dit nie 'n lisensie "
"verleen om hersienings te maak nie, dan is daar 'n groter gevaar as dié van "
"kettery."

msgid ""
"The bigger danger is that the copyright holder holds on to the Bible, or "
"disappears, or dies, or fails to be a good steward of it."
msgstr ""
"Die groter gevaar is dat die outeursregbesitter die Bybel vashou, of "
"verdwyn, of sterf, of nie 'n goeie rentmeester daarvan is nie."

msgid "Nobody would be allowed to improve or update the text."
msgstr ""
"Niemand sal toegelaat word om die teks te verbeter of op te dateer nie."

msgid "Trust God."
msgstr "Vertrou God."

msgid "He takes care of His Word."
msgstr "Hy sorg vir Sy Woord."

msgid "He deals with anyone who might abuse it."
msgstr "Hy handel met enigiemand wat dit dalk kan misbruik."

msgid "The Bible Society says:"
msgstr "Die Bybelgenootskap sê:"

msgid ""
"We own copyright, not in any way to restrict distribution, but to preserve "
"the text."
msgstr ""
"Ons besit outeursreg, nie om verspreiding op enige manier te beperk nie, "
"maar om die teks te bewaar."

msgid "Protecting the text may at times restrict distribution."
msgstr "Die beskerming van die teks kan soms verspreiding beperk."

msgid ""
"For example, the Bible must be distributed by us, or under our supervision."
msgstr ""
"Die Bybel moet byvoorbeeld deur ons, of onder ons toesig, versprei word."

msgid "We have made a big investment in the Bible."
msgstr "Ons het 'n groot belegging in die Bybel gemaak."

msgid "Nobody may improve it without our authority."
msgstr "Niemand mag dit sonder ons gesag verbeter nie."

msgid ""
"If anybody gives us details as to where the Bible can be improved, they can "
"improve it, but only when we agree."
msgstr ""
"As iemand ons besonderhede gee oor waar die Bybel verbeter kan word, kan "
"hulle dit verbeter, maar slegs wanneer ons saamstem."

msgid "This Bible is our property."
msgstr "Hierdie Bybel is ons eiendom."

msgid "We share it."
msgstr "Ons deel dit."

msgid "It is not entirely ours, so there is a shared property."
msgstr "Dit is nie geheel en al ons s'n nie, dus is daar 'n gedeelde eiendom."

msgid "The Free Documentation License is good in an ideal world."
msgstr "Die Vrye Dokumentasielisensie is goed in 'n ideale wêreld."

msgid ""
"But the world is evil, so we need a license where we can protect the "
"integrity of the text."
msgstr ""
"Maar die wêreld is sleg, dus het ons 'n lisensie nodig waar ons die "
"integriteit van die teks kan beskerm."

msgid "The proponent of the free Bible says:"
msgstr "Die voorstander van die vrye Bybel sê:"

msgid "A free license enables spreading the Word of God more quickly."
msgstr ""
"'n Vrye lisensie maak dit moontlik om die Woord van God vinniger te "
"versprei."

msgid "The Bible Society has made such a reliable and good Bible."
msgstr "Die Bybelgenootskap het so 'n betroubare en goeie Bybel gemaak."

msgid "Is it not worthy of being spread as far and wide as possible?"
msgstr ""
"Is dit nie die moeite werd om so wyd en wyd as moontlik versprei te word "
"nie?"

msgid "A restrictive license confines the Word to one publisher, one channel."
msgstr "'n Beperkende lisensie beperk die Woord tot een uitgewer, een kanaal."

msgid "A free license opens up the Word to being spread by more channels."
msgstr ""
"'n Vrye lisensie maak die Woord oop om deur meer kanale versprei te word."

msgid ""
"If the license is restrictive, it is not the bad people who are afraid of "
"illegally copying the Word of God, making changes, then publish it."
msgstr ""
"As die lisensie beperkend is, is dit nie die slegte mense wat bang is om die"
" Woord van God onwettig te kopieer, veranderinge aan te bring, en dit dan te"
" publiseer nie."

msgid ""
"But it's the good people who would be worried to violate copyright law when "
"spreading the Word, thinking that God's blessing cannot be on something "
"illegal."
msgstr ""
"Maar dit is die goeie mense wat bekommerd sal wees om outeursreg te oortree "
"wanneer hulle die Woord versprei, omdat hulle dink dat God se seën nie op "
"iets onwettigs kan wees nie."

msgid ""
"The free license does not aid bad people much, but it assists good people in"
" many ways."
msgstr ""
"Die vrye lisensie help nie slegte mense veel nie, maar dit help goeie mense "
"op baie maniere."

msgid ""
"A restrictive license does not stop heretics in any way, but it stops good "
"people from spreading the Word."
msgstr ""
"'n Beperkende lisensie stop op geen manier ketters nie, maar dit keer goeie "
"mense om die Woord te versprei."

msgid "The restrictive Bible Society says:"
msgstr "Die beperkende Bybelgenootskap sê:"

msgid "If you revise our Bible, we'll see you in court."
msgstr "As u ons Bybel hersien, sien ons u in die hof."

msgid "The free and open Bible Society says:"
msgstr "Die vrye en oop Bybelgenootskap sê:"

msgid ""
"If you revise and spread our Bible, we thank God for opening another channel"
" for distribution."
msgstr ""
"As u ons Bybel hersien en versprei, dank ons God dat Hy nog 'n kanaal vir "
"verspreiding oopmaak."

msgid "God wanted property rights to be there for the benefit of humans."
msgstr "God wou hê eiendomsregte moet daar wees tot voordeel van mense."

msgid "But did he also want copyright on Bibles?"
msgstr "Maar het Hy ook outeursreg op Bybels gewil?"

msgid "Show from the Word where this is the case."
msgstr "Toon uit die Woord waar dit die geval is."

msgid "Install Bibledit Cloud on Linux"
msgstr "Installeer Bibledit Cloud op Linux"

msgid "Bibledit Cloud can be installed in several ways."
msgstr "Bibledit Cloud kan op verskeie maniere geïnstalleer word."

msgid "Installation from packages."
msgstr "Installasie vanaf pakkette."

msgid "Installation from source."
msgstr "Installasie vanaf bronkode."

msgid "Licenses"
msgstr "Lisensies"

msgid "Typesetting in Adobe InDesign CS5.5"
msgstr "Setwerk in Adobe InDesign CS5.5"

msgid ""
"See the online help about typesetting for more information and general "
"principles."
msgstr ""
"Sien die aanlyn hulp oor setwerk vir meer inligting en algemene beginsels."

msgid "Chapter numbers in drop caps"
msgstr "Hoofstuknommers in sierletters"

msgid ""
"Bibledit normally exports chapter numbers in bigger font in a text frame."
msgstr ""
"Bibledit voer gewoonlik hoofstuknommers uit in groter lettergrootte in 'n "
"tekskader."

msgid "In InDesign it is helpful to have these in drop caps."
msgstr "In InDesign is dit nuttig om dit in sierletters te hê."

msgid "Go to Bibledit, menu Export."
msgstr "Gaan na Bibledit, kieslys Voer uit."

msgid "There is a setting for using frames in the drop caps. Switch it off."
msgstr ""
"Daar is 'n instelling vir die gebruik van rame in die sierletters. Skakel "
"dit af."

msgid "Do a fresh export."
msgstr "Doen 'n nuwe uitvoer."

msgid "Creating a new document"
msgstr "Skep 'n nuwe dokument"

msgid "Typesetting in InDesign starts with creating a new document."
msgstr "Setwerk in InDesign begin met die skep van 'n nuwe dokument."

msgid "Choose menu File / New / Document, or press Ctrl-N."
msgstr "Kies kieslys Lêer / Nuut / Dokument, of druk Ctrl-N."

msgid "In the New Document dialog, make some settings."
msgstr "Maak in die Nuwe Dokument-dialoog 'n paar instellings."

msgid "Facing Pages: on."
msgstr "Teenoorstaande bladsye: aan."

msgid "Page width: 138 mm."
msgstr "Bladsybreedte: 138 mm."

msgid "Page height: 210 mm."
msgstr "Bladsyhoogte: 210 mm."

msgid "Number of columns: 2."
msgstr "Aantal kolomme: 2."

msgid "Gutter: 4.2 mm."
msgstr "Kolomruimte: 4.2 mm."

msgid "Top, Bottom and Outside margins: 10 mm."
msgstr "Bo-, Onder- en Buitekantlyne: 10 mm."

msgid "Untick the option to set all margins the same."
msgstr "Ontmerk die opsie om alle kantlyne dieselfde te stel."

msgid "Inside margin: 12 mm."
msgstr "Binnekantlyn: 12 mm."

msgid ""
"Click Save Preset, and save the settings as 'Ndebele'. Next time, use this "
"preset to quickly make another new document with the same settings as this "
"one."
msgstr ""
"Klik op Stoor voorafinstelling, en stoor die instellings as 'Ndebele'. "
"Gebruik volgende keer hierdie voorafinstelling om vinnig nog 'n nuwe "
"dokument met dieselfde instellings as hierdie een te maak."

msgid "Click OK to create the new document."
msgstr "Klik OK om die nuwe dokument te skep."

msgid "Setting up the baseline grid"
msgstr "Stel die basislynrooster op"

msgid "All our text will stick to the baseline grid."
msgstr "Al ons teks sal by die basislynrooster hou."

msgid "This is a key factor to good typography."
msgstr "Dit is 'n sleutelfaktor vir goeie tipografie."

msgid "My leading is 12 points, and I will set up a grid to reflect this."
msgstr ""
"My reëlspasiëring is 12 punte, en ek sal 'n rooster opstel om dit te "
"weerspieël."

msgid "Go to menu Edit / Preferences / Grids."
msgstr "Gaan na kieslys Wysig / Voorkeure / Roosters."

msgid "Start the baseline grid at 0 mm relative to the top margin."
msgstr "Begin die basislynrooster by 0 mm relatief tot die boonste kantlyn."

msgid "Increment it every 12 points."
msgstr "Verhoog dit elke 12 punte."

msgid "Press OK. The grid is now set up."
msgstr "Druk OK. Die rooster is nou opgestel."

msgid ""
"Optionally, to make it visible, go to menu View / Grids and Guides / Show "
"Baseline Grid."
msgstr ""
"Opsioneel, om dit sigbaar te maak, gaan na kieslys Bekyk / Roosters en "
"Leidrade / Wys basislynrooster."

msgid "Placing text"
msgstr "Plaas teks"

msgid "I am going to show how to place Bible text in InDesign."
msgstr "Ek gaan wys hoe om Bybelteks in InDesign te plaas."

msgid "The text is available from Bibledit as OpenDocument files."
msgstr "Die teks is as OpenDocument-lêers van Bibledit beskikbaar."

msgid ""
"Open the book of Genesis, the version with text and note citations, in "
"OpenOffice."
msgstr ""
"Maak die boek Genesis, die weergawe met teks en nota-aanhalings, in "
"OpenOffice oop."

msgid "Save it as a Microsoft Word 97-2003 (.doc) document."
msgstr "Stoor dit as 'n Microsoft Word 97-2003 (.doc) dokument."

msgid "Create a new document in InDesign."
msgstr "Skep 'n nuwe dokument in InDesign."

msgid "Go to menu File / Place, or press Ctrl-D."
msgstr "Gaan na kieslys Lêer / Plaas, of druk Ctrl-D."

msgid "Select the document in MS Word (.doc) format."
msgstr "Kies die dokument in MS Word (.doc) formaat."

msgid ""
"Move the cursor through the document in InDesign. Notice that the cursor "
"shows some of the text to be placed."
msgstr ""
"Beweeg die wyser deur die dokument in InDesign. Let op dat die wyser 'n deel"
" van die teks wys wat geplaas gaan word."

msgid ""
"Move the cursor to the corner of the first column where the text will start."
" Click there. Notice that the first bit of the text will be placed in the "
"first column."
msgstr ""
"Beweeg die wyser na die hoek van die eerste kolom waar die teks sal begin. "
"Klik daar. Let op dat die eerste bietjie van die teks in die eerste kolom "
"geplaas sal word."

msgid ""
"There is much more text than what fits in just one column. This extra text "
"is not visible. What is visible, though, is a red plus near the end of the "
"first column. This shows that more text is available."
msgstr ""
"Daar is baie meer teks as wat in net een kolom pas. Hierdie ekstra teks is "
"nie sigbaar nie. Wat wel sigbaar is, is 'n rooi plusteken naby die einde van"
" die eerste kolom. Dit wys dat meer teks beskikbaar is."

msgid "I would like to place this extra text in the second column."
msgstr "Ek wil hierdie ekstra teks in die tweede kolom plaas."

msgid ""
"Click the Selection Tool or press V. The cursor changes to a selection "
"arrow."
msgstr "Klik die Keurgereedskap of druk V. Die wyser verander na 'n keurpyl."

msgid ""
"Select the first column, and then click the red plus near the end of the "
"first column. Notice that the cursor will now show some text."
msgstr ""
"Kies die eerste kolom, en klik dan die rooi plusteken naby die einde van die"
" eerste kolom. Let op dat die wyser nou 'n bietjie teks sal wys."

msgid ""
"Place this text in the second column, in the same way as it was placed in "
"the first column."
msgstr ""
"Plaas hierdie teks in die tweede kolom, op dieselfde manier as wat dit in "
"die eerste kolom geplaas is."

msgid ""
"There is still more text than fits in the second column. I estimate that "
"there is enough text to fill many pages."
msgstr ""
"Daar is nog steeds meer teks as wat in die tweede kolom pas. Ek skat daar is"
" genoeg teks om baie bladsye te vul."

msgid ""
"I am going to insert an extra page, so that we get more space to place the "
"text."
msgstr ""
"Ek gaan 'n ekstra bladsy invoeg, sodat ons meer ruimte kry om die teks te "
"plaas."

msgid ""
"To add blank pages, I need to have the Pages palette visible. If the Pages "
"palette is not visible, choose Window > Pages to open the palette."
msgstr ""
"Om leë bladsye by te voeg, moet ek die Bladsye-palet sigbaar hê. As die "
"Bladsye-palet nie sigbaar is nie, kies Venster > Bladsye om die palet oop te"
" maak."

msgid ""
"In the Pages palette, click Create new page. A new page will be added. This "
"is page 2. Press F12 to close the palette."
msgstr ""
"Klik in die Bladsye-palet op Skep nuwe bladsy. 'n Nuwe bladsy sal bygevoeg "
"word. Dit is bladsy 2. Druk F12 om die palet toe te maak."

msgid ""
"Page 2 shows guides for two columns. I can fill these with text in the "
"manner as described above."
msgstr ""
"Bladsy 2 wys leidrade vir twee kolomme. Ek kan hierdie met teks vul op die "
"manier wat hierbo beskryf is."

msgid ""
"I can then add as many pages as are needed, and fill each page with text."
msgstr ""
"Ek kan dan soveel bladsye byvoeg as wat nodig is, en elke bladsy met teks "
"vul."

msgid "Span headlines across columns"
msgstr "Strek opskrifte oor kolomme"

msgid ""
"The headline I have in this example is 'The first book of Moses called "
"Genesis'. I'd like it to span across the two columns."
msgstr ""
"Die opskrif wat ek in hierdie voorbeeld het, is 'Die eerste boek van Moses "
"genaamd Genesis'. Ek wil hê dit moet oor die twee kolomme strek."

msgid ""
"Select the left column, and drag the top to make it shorter, so creating "
"space above it."
msgstr ""
"Kies die linkerkolom, en sleep die bokant om dit korter te maak, en sodoende"
" ruimte daarbo te skep."

msgid "Do the same with the right column."
msgstr "Doen dieselfde met die regterkolom."

msgid ""
"Select the text 'The first book of Moses called Genesis'. Cut it to the "
"clipboard."
msgstr ""
"Kies die teks 'Die eerste boek van Moses genaamd Genesis'. Sny dit na die "
"knipbord."

msgid "Click the Type tool or type Escape T."
msgstr "Klik die Teksgereedskap of tik Escape T."

msgid ""
"Create a new text box above the two columns. Let it span across the two "
"columns. Estimate the size it needs to be."
msgstr ""
"Skep 'n nuwe tekskas bokant die twee kolomme. Laat dit oor die twee kolomme "
"strek. Skat die grootte wat dit moet wees."

msgid "Paste the text into that text box."
msgstr "Plak die teks in daardie tekskas."

msgid ""
"Resize the text box so it looks smart. Then resize both columns so that all "
"looks good."
msgstr ""
"Verander die grootte van die tekskas sodat dit netjies lyk. Verander dan die"
" grootte van albei kolomme sodat alles goed lyk."

msgid "Making text align to the grid"
msgstr "Lyn teks met die rooster uit"

msgid "Text aligned to the grid is key to good typesetting."
msgstr ""
"Teks wat met die rooster uitgelyn is, is die sleutel tot goeie setwerk."

msgid "Select all text you would like to stick to the baseline grid."
msgstr "Kies alle teks wat u aan die basislynrooster wil laat hou."

msgid "Go to menu Type / Paragraph, or press Alt-Ctrl-T."
msgstr "Gaan na kieslys Teks / Paragraaf, of druk Alt-Ctrl-T."

msgid ""
"Press the Align to baseline grid button in the bottom right hand corner."
msgstr ""
"Druk die Lyn uit met basislynrooster-knoppie in die onderste regterhoek."

msgid ""
"The leading of the text should be equal to the baseline grid. If the leading"
" of the text is bigger, then it is like as if you have double line spacing."
msgstr ""
"Die reëlspasiëring van die teks moet gelyk wees aan die basislynrooster. As "
"die reëlspasiëring van die teks groter is, is dit asof u dubbelspasiëring "
"het."

msgid "Total page count"
msgstr "Totale bladsytelling"

msgid ""
"The publisher may set limits to the number of pages the typeset Bible may "
"contain."
msgstr ""
"Die uitgewer kan perke stel op die aantal bladsye wat die gesette Bybel mag "
"bevat."

msgid ""
"In this example, we expect an entire Bible, with singable Psalms added as an"
" appendix, to contain no more than 2000 pages. Normal range is 1500 to 1800 "
"pages."
msgstr ""
"In hierdie voorbeeld verwag ons dat 'n hele Bybel, met singbare Psalms as 'n"
" bylae bygevoeg, nie meer as 2000 bladsye sal bevat nie. Die normale reeks "
"is 1500 tot 1800 bladsye."

msgid "We suppose that the singable Psalms take up no more than 200 pages."
msgstr ""
"Ons veronderstel dat die singbare Psalms nie meer as 200 bladsye beslaan "
"nie."

msgid ""
"Usually the inclusion of the singable Psalms in a Bible will add about 10 "
"percent to the number of pages."
msgstr ""
"Gewoonlik voeg die insluiting van die singbare Psalms in 'n Bybel ongeveer "
"10 persent by die aantal bladsye."

msgid ""
"The Bible will have footnotes and crossreferences, all lumped together into "
"a single textframe at the bottom of each page."
msgstr ""
"Die Bybel sal voetnotas en kruisverwysings hê, almal saamgevat in 'n enkele "
"tekskader onderaan elke bladsy."

msgid "Let us now measure how many pages the notes are likely to take up."
msgstr "Kom ons meet nou hoeveel bladsye die notas waarskynlik sal beslaan."

msgid ""
"Open the file with all notes in LibreOffice. It is 00_Bible_notes.odt. Save "
"it in the correct format for InDesign."
msgstr ""
"Maak die lêer met alle notas in LibreOffice oop. Dit is 00_Bible_notes.odt. "
"Stoor dit in die korrekte formaat vir InDesign."

msgid ""
"Place the text as described above. But I am going to use Autoflow this time."
" Autoflow will automatically create new text boxes and new page till all "
"text has been placed. This allows us quickly to see how many pages the notes"
" will take up."
msgstr ""
"Plaas die teks soos hierbo beskryf. Maar ek gaan hierdie keer Outovloei "
"gebruik. Outovloei sal outomaties nuwe tekskaste en nuwe bladsye skep totdat"
" alle teks geplaas is. Dit laat ons toe om vinnig te sien hoeveel bladsye "
"die notas sal beslaan."

msgid "This is how to use Autoflow."
msgstr "Dit is hoe om Outovloei te gebruik."

msgid ""
"When you are about the click where you want the text to go, keep the Shift "
"key down."
msgstr ""
"Wanneer u op die punt is om te klik waar u die teks wil hê, hou die Shift-"
"sleutel af."

msgid ""
"I can now roughly see the total number of pages that the notes will take up."
msgstr ""
"Ek kan nou grofweg die totale aantal bladsye sien wat die notas sal beslaan."

msgid "This is sufficient for an estimate."
msgstr "Dit is voldoende vir 'n skatting."

msgid ""
"Let us now find out how many pages the main text body is likely to take up."
msgstr ""
"Kom ons vind nou uit hoeveel bladsye die hoofteksliggaam waarskynlik sal "
"beslaan."

msgid "The text is in the file called 00_Bible_text_and_note_citations.odt."
msgstr "Die teks is in die lêer genaamd 00_Bible_text_and_note_citations.odt."

msgid "Place this text and use Autoflow."
msgstr "Plaas hierdie teks en gebruik Outovloei."

msgid ""
"It appears that, on my system, all text cannot be placed at once. It will "
"cut off after some point."
msgstr ""
"Dit blyk dat, op my stelsel, alle teks nie gelyktydig geplaas kan word nie. "
"Dit sal na 'n sekere punt afgesny word."

msgid "I will place 01_Genesis_text_and_note_citations.odt instead."
msgstr "Ek sal in plaas daarvan 01_Genesis_text_and_note_citations.odt plaas."

msgid ""
"I can now roughly see the total number of pages that the text of Genesis "
"will take up."
msgstr ""
"Ek kan nou grofweg die totale aantal bladsye sien wat die teks van Genesis "
"sal beslaan."

msgid ""
"The size of the whole Bible is about 22 times more than the size of Genesis."
msgstr ""
"Die grootte van die hele Bybel is ongeveer 22 keer meer as die grootte van "
"Genesis."

msgid ""
"The font is of particular influence on the page count. This is not dealt "
"with here."
msgstr ""
"Die lettertipe het besondere invloed op die bladsytelling. Dit word nie hier"
" behandel nie."

msgid "Editing a paragraph style"
msgstr "Wysig 'n paragraafstyl"

msgid ""
"After exporting USFM text to OpenDocument, and placing this text into "
"InDesign, the USFM styles appear in InDesign."
msgstr ""
"Nadat USFM-teks na OpenDocument uitgevoer is, en hierdie teks in InDesign "
"geplaas is, verskyn die USFM-style in InDesign."

msgid ""
"For example, normal paragraphs usually have style 'p', and section heading "
"'s'."
msgstr ""
"Normale paragrawe het byvoorbeeld gewoonlik styl 'p', en afdelingsopskrifte "
"'s'."

msgid ""
"If you like to update a paragraph style, you may update each section heading"
" individually, but this is a lot of work. It is faster to update the style "
"for 's', so that this updates all paragraphs that have this style."
msgstr ""
"As u 'n paragraafstyl wil opdateer, kan u elke afdelingsopskrif individueel "
"opdateer, maar dit is baie werk. Dit is vinniger om die styl vir 's' op te "
"dateer, sodat dit alle paragrawe wat hierdie styl het, opdateer."

msgid ""
"To update a paragraph style, place the cursor in it, and on the palette "
"choose Paragraph Styles. Right-click the style you want and choose Edit."
msgstr ""
"Om 'n paragraafstyl op te dateer, plaas die wyser daarin, en kies "
"Paragraafstyle op die palet. Regsklik die styl wat u wil hê en kies Wysig."

msgid ""
"Section headings look better after ticking ‘Balance ragged lines’ in the "
"paragraph options."
msgstr ""
"Afdelingsopskrifte lyk beter nadat u 'Balanseer onegalige reëls' in die "
"paragraafopsies gemerk het."

msgid "Running headers"
msgstr "Lopende opskrifte"

msgid ""
"The Bible will have running headers. The headers contain the page number "
"near the inside margin. At the right margin it shows book and chapter "
"numbers on that page."
msgstr ""
"Die Bybel sal lopende opskrifte hê. Die opskrifte bevat die bladsynommer "
"naby die binnekantlyn. By die regterkantlyn wys dit boek- en hoofstuknommers"
" op daardie bladsy."

msgid "Enter the page numbers on the master pages."
msgstr "Voer die bladsynommers op die meesterbladsye in."

msgid "On the Pages palette, double-click the master pages."
msgstr "Dubbelklik op die Bladsye-palet die meesterbladsye."

msgid ""
"On the left master page, create a text frame, and enter the page number at "
"the inside margin."
msgstr ""
"Skep op die linker meesterbladsy 'n tekskader, en voer die bladsynommer by "
"die binnekantlyn in."

msgid ""
"Page numbers can be found in menu Type / Insert Special Character / Marker /"
" Current Page Number."
msgstr ""
"Bladsynommers kan gevind word in kieslys Teks / Voeg spesiale karakter in / "
"Merker / Huidige bladsynommer."

msgid ""
"On the right master page, create a text frame, and enter the page number at "
"the inside margin too."
msgstr ""
"Skep op die regter meesterbladsy 'n tekskader, en voer ook die bladsynommer "
"by die binnekantlyn in."

msgid ""
"On page 1, create a new text frame at the top, and put the book and chapter "
"at the outside margin."
msgstr ""
"Skep op bladsy 1 'n nuwe tekskader bo-aan, en plaas die boek en hoofstuk by "
"die buitekantlyn."

msgid "This text frame can be copied to each odd page as it is generated."
msgstr ""
"Hierdie tekskader kan na elke onewe bladsy gekopieer word soos dit "
"gegenereer word."

msgid "The same applies for page 2, and any subsequent even pages."
msgstr "Dieselfde geld vir bladsy 2, en enige daaropvolgende ewe bladsye."

msgid "The page where a book starts normally does not display a page number."
msgstr ""
"Die bladsy waar 'n boek begin, vertoon normaalweg nie 'n bladsynommer nie."

msgid "In order to do that, apply master page [None] to that particular page."
msgstr ""
"Om dit te doen, pas meesterbladsy [Geen] op daardie spesifieke bladsy toe."

msgid "Space between drop caps and text"
msgstr "Spasie tussen sierletters en teks"

msgid ""
"It may be visually pleasant to have some space between the drop caps chapter"
" numbers and the text beside it."
msgstr ""
"Dit kan visueel aangenaam wees om 'n bietjie spasie tussen die "
"hoofstuknommers in sierletters en die teks daarnaas te hê."

msgid ""
"All that is needed is a fixed space after the chapter numbers. Pick any one "
"from a hair space to an em space. The number of characters in drop caps is "
"now increased by one. Set this value in the drop cap settings. All lines "
"after the first will automatically line up."
msgstr ""
"Al wat nodig is, is 'n vaste spasie na die hoofstuknommers. Kies enige een "
"van 'n haarspasie tot 'n em-spasie. Die aantal karakters in sierletters word"
" nou met een verhoog. Stel hierdie waarde in die sierletter-instellings. "
"Alle reëls na die eerste sal outomaties belyn."

msgid "Managing widows or orphans"
msgstr "Bestuur weduwees of weeskinders"

msgid ""
"Widows and orphans are words or short lines at the beginning or end of a "
"paragraph, which are left dangling at the top or bottom of a column, "
"separated from the rest of the paragraph."
msgstr ""
"Weduwees en weeskinders is woorde of kort reëls aan die begin of einde van "
"'n paragraaf, wat bo- of onderaan 'n kolom bly hang, geskei van die res van "
"die paragraaf."

msgid ""
"There is some disagreement about the definitions of widow and orphan; what "
"one calls a widow the other calls an orphan."
msgstr ""
"Daar is 'n mate van onenigheid oor die definisies van weduwee en weeskind; "
"wat die een 'n weduwee noem, noem die ander 'n weeskind."

msgid "There are some ways to avoid widows or orphans."
msgstr "Daar is 'n paar maniere om weduwees of weeskinders te vermy."

msgid ""
"- Adjusting the spacing between words to produce tighter or looser "
"paragraphs."
msgstr ""
"- Pas die spasiëring tussen woorde aan om stywer of losser paragrawe te "
"lewer."

msgid ""
"- Adjusting the tracking of the text. This is the overall spacing of the "
"letters in a paragraph or on a line. With a good font in justified "
"paragraphs this can usually be adjusted by up to -25 or +15 without it "
"looking too out of place."
msgstr ""
"- Pas die spoorspasiëring van die teks aan. Dit is die algehele spasiëring "
"van die letters in 'n paragraaf of op 'n reël. Met 'n goeie lettertipe in "
"uitgevulde paragrawe kan dit gewoonlik tot -25 of +15 aangepas word sonder "
"dat dit te misplaas lyk."

msgid "- Adjusting the hyphenation of words within the paragraph."
msgstr "- Pas die woordafbreking binne die paragraaf aan."

msgid "- Forcing a word down onto the next line using a soft return."
msgstr "- Dwing 'n woord na die volgende reël met 'n sagte terugkeer."

msgid "Scripting"
msgstr "Skripte"

msgid "Here is a sample script."
msgstr "Hier is 'n voorbeeldskrip."

msgid "It runs in InDesign."
msgstr "Dit loop in InDesign."

msgid "It shows how to replace text, and how to update the formatting."
msgstr ""
"Dit wys hoe om teks te vervang, en hoe om die formatering op te dateer."

msgid "Install Bibledit on Ubuntu"
msgstr "Installeer Bibledit op Ubuntu"

msgid "Follow the steps below to install Bibledit."
msgstr "Volg die stappe hieronder om Bibledit te installeer."

msgid "Open a terminal."
msgstr "Maak 'n terminaal oop."

msgid "On older versions of Ubuntu, or to get updated Bibledit software:"
msgstr ""
"Op ouer weergawes van Ubuntu, of om opgedateerde Bibledit-sagteware te kry:"

msgid "Add the Bibledit repository:"
msgstr "Voeg die Bibledit-bewaarplek by:"

msgid "As of Ubuntu 18.04, the above is no longer needed."
msgstr "Vanaf Ubuntu 18.04 is bogenoemde nie meer nodig nie."

msgid "Read the repository:"
msgstr "Lees die bewaarplek:"

msgid "Install Bibledit:"
msgstr "Installeer Bibledit:"

msgid "Bibledit can be started from the menu."
msgstr "Bibledit kan vanaf die kieslys begin word."

msgid "More information:"
msgstr "Meer inligting:"

msgid "The Notes are an important part of Consultations."
msgstr "Die Notas is 'n belangrike deel van Konsultasies."

msgid ""
"The notes help to record the discussions with consultants and other people."
msgstr ""
"Die notas help om die besprekings met konsultante en ander mense aan te "
"teken."

msgid ""
"Normally, when going to the Consultation Notes, you will see a list of "
"notes."
msgstr ""
"Normaalweg, wanneer u na die Konsultasienotas gaan, sal u 'n lys van notas "
"sien."

msgid "It would say, for example: Displaying notes 1 - 5 / 5."
msgstr "Dit sal byvoorbeeld sê: Vertoon notas 1 - 5 / 5."

msgid "This means that it would display notes 1 to 5, out of 5 notes total."
msgstr "Dit beteken dat dit notas 1 tot 5 vertoon, uit 5 notas in totaal."

msgid "You can edit the display."
msgstr "U kan die vertoning wysig."

msgid ""
"That means that you can edit the number of notes that will display in that "
"list."
msgstr ""
"Dit beteken dat u die aantal notas kan wysig wat in daardie lys sal vertoon."

msgid "Clicking [edit] takes you to a new page, called Edit Notes Display."
msgstr ""
"As u op [wysig] klik, neem dit u na 'n nuwe bladsy, genaamd Wysig "
"notavertoning."

msgid ""
"This enables you to edit how the notes will be displayed, and how many."
msgstr ""
"Dit stel u in staat om te wysig hoe die notas vertoon sal word, en hoeveel."

msgid "The first thing that you can edit is how many notes will be selected."
msgstr "Die eerste ding wat u kan wysig, is hoeveel notas gekies sal word."

msgid ""
"If you select notes that refer to any passage, then notes will be selected "
"that refer to any passage, from Genesis to Revelation."
msgstr ""
"As u notas kies wat na enige gedeelte verwys, sal notas gekies word wat na "
"enige gedeelte verwys, van Genesis tot Openbaring."

msgid ""
"But when you select notes that refer to the current verse, then only those "
"notes will be selected that refer to the currently opened verse."
msgstr ""
"Maar wanneer u notas kies wat na die huidige vers verwys, sal slegs daardie "
"notas gekies word wat na die tans oop vers verwys."

msgid ""
"In case you have Genesis 2.2 open in the navigator, then only notes that "
"refer to that particular verse are displayed."
msgstr ""
"As u Genesis 2.2 in die navigeerder oop het, word slegs notas wat na daardie"
" spesifieke vers verwys, vertoon."

msgid ""
"If you select notes that have been edited at any time, then all notes would "
"be selected."
msgstr ""
"As u notas kies wat te eniger tyd geredigeer is, sal alle notas gekies word."

msgid ""
"But when you select notes that have been edited on Today, then only today's "
"notes are displayed."
msgstr ""
"Maar wanneer u notas kies wat Vandag geredigeer is, word slegs vandag se "
"notas vertoon."

msgid ""
"The note selection mechanism combines all selection methods that have been "
"set."
msgstr "Die notakeuse-meganisme kombineer alle keusemetodes wat gestel is."

msgid ""
"If you select notes that refer to the current verse, for example, and that "
"have been edited today, and only those notes that both refer to the current "
"verse, and that also have been edited today, are displayed."
msgstr ""
"As u byvoorbeeld notas kies wat na die huidige vers verwys, en wat vandag "
"geredigeer is, word slegs daardie notas vertoon wat beide na die huidige "
"vers verwys, en ook vandag geredigeer is."

msgid "There are other notes selection mechanisms as well."
msgstr "Daar is ook ander notakeuse-meganismes."

msgid "See the relevant page for all selection mechanisms."
msgstr "Sien die relevante bladsy vir alle keuse-meganismes."

msgid ""
"Things should be plain and there should be no need for any further "
"information."
msgstr ""
"Dinge behoort eenvoudig te wees en daar behoort geen behoefte aan enige "
"verdere inligting te wees nie."

msgid ""
"One thing that would need explanation would be the mechanism that selects "
"notes that contain certain text."
msgstr ""
"Een ding wat verduideliking sal benodig, is die meganisme wat notas kies wat"
" sekere teks bevat."

msgid "This is intended to be used to search notes for text."
msgstr "Dit is bedoel om gebruik te word om notas vir teks te deursoek."

msgid ""
"If you select notes that contain Any text, then searching for text in the "
"note is not done."
msgstr ""
"As u notas kies wat Enige teks bevat, word daar nie na teks in die nota "
"gesoek nie."

msgid ""
"Searching for text can be done by selecting notes that contain specific "
"words or text."
msgstr ""
"Soek na teks kan gedoen word deur notas te kies wat spesifieke woorde of "
"teks bevat."

msgid ""
"When you select this option, you will see that an entry becomes visible."
msgstr ""
"Wanneer u hierdie opsie kies, sal u sien dat 'n invoerveld sigbaar word."

msgid "Search text should be entered there."
msgstr "Soekteks moet daar ingevoer word."

msgid "Then the Save button should be pressed."
msgstr "Dan moet die Stoor-knoppie gedruk word."

msgid "This is to save that search text."
msgstr "Dit is om daardie soekteks te stoor."

msgid ""
" Or just pressing Enter while the cursor is in that entry will do also."
msgstr ""
" Of net Enter druk terwyl die wyser in daardie invoerveld is, sal ook werk."

msgid ""
"When you search for, for example, 'house', then notes that contain the word "
"'house' will be selected."
msgstr ""
"Wanneer u byvoorbeeld na 'huis' soek, sal notas wat die woord 'huis' bevat, "
"gekies word."

msgid ""
"Notes that contain the word 'houses' (in plural) would not be selected."
msgstr ""
"Notas wat die woord 'huise' (in meervoud) bevat, sal nie gekies word nie."

msgid "To select this plural form, you can use wildcards."
msgstr "Om hierdie meervoudsvorm te kies, kan u jokertekens gebruik."

msgid "Instead of entering 'house, enter 'house*'."
msgstr "In plaas daarvan om 'huis' in te voer, voer 'huis*' in."

msgid "Notice the asterisk."
msgstr "Let op die sterretjie."

msgid "This will select notes that contains the word 'house' or 'houses."
msgstr "Dit sal notas kies wat die woord 'huis' of 'huise' bevat."

msgid "You can also enter two or more words to search for."
msgstr "U kan ook twee of meer woorde invoer om voor te soek."

msgid ""
"The search routine will then do its best to select these notes that contain "
"some or all of these words."
msgstr ""
"Die soekroetine sal dan sy bes doen om daardie notas te kies wat sommige of "
"al hierdie woorde bevat."

msgid ""
"Notes that contain all words are given first, and notes that contains only "
"one or a few of the words will be given later."
msgstr ""
"Notas wat al die woorde bevat, word eerste gegee, en notas wat net een of 'n"
" paar van die woorde bevat, word later gegee."

msgid ""
"If you select notes that refer to the current verse, and then also search "
"for some text, then only the notes that refer to the current verse would be "
"searched."
msgstr ""
"As u notas kies wat na die huidige vers verwys, en dan ook na 'n bietjie "
"teks soek, sal slegs die notas wat na die huidige vers verwys, deursoek "
"word."

msgid "It is important to be aware of this."
msgstr "Dit is belangrik om hiervan bewus te wees."

msgid ""
"At times one may search for words or phrases, and get zero results, yet he "
"is sure that there should be some results."
msgstr ""
"Soms soek 'n mens na woorde of frases, en kry nul resultate, maar is seker "
"dat daar resultate behoort te wees."

msgid ""
"This would happen because the user does not search the whole Bible, but only"
" the current verse."
msgstr ""
"Dit sal gebeur omdat die gebruiker nie die hele Bybel deursoek nie, maar net"
" die huidige vers."

msgid "The same applies to other selection mechanisms."
msgstr "Dieselfde geld vir ander keuse-meganismes."

msgid ""
"Therefore, when searching notes for text, you may want to set all other "
"selection mechanisms to Any."
msgstr ""
"Daarom, wanneer u notas vir teks deursoek, wil u dalk alle ander keuse-"
"meganismes op Enige stel."

msgid "There is more that can be said about searching notes."
msgstr "Daar is meer wat oor die deursoek van notas gesê kan word."

msgid "The wildcard operator already has been mentioned."
msgstr "Die jokerteken-operateur is reeds genoem."

msgid "Here is a list of possible operators:"
msgstr "Hier is 'n lys van moontlike operateurs:"

msgid ""
"By default, when no operator specified, the word is optional, but the result"
" that contain it will be rated higher."
msgstr ""
"By verstek, wanneer geen operateur gespesifiseer is nie, is die woord "
"opsioneel, maar die resultate wat dit bevat, sal hoër gegradeer word."

msgid ""
"A leading plus sign indicates that this word must be present in every result"
" returned."
msgstr ""
"'n Voorafgaande plusteken dui aan dat hierdie woord in elke resultaat wat "
"teruggegee word, teenwoordig moet wees."

msgid ""
"A leading minus sign indicates that this word must not be present in any "
"result returned."
msgstr ""
"'n Voorafgaande minusteken dui aan dat hierdie woord nie in enige resultaat "
"wat teruggegee word, teenwoordig mag wees nie."

msgid ""
"A leading tilde acts as a negation operator, causing the word's contribution"
" to the result relevance to be negative."
msgstr ""
"'n Voorafgaande tilde tree op as 'n negasie-operateur, wat veroorsaak dat "
"die woord se bydrae tot die resultaatrelevansie negatief is."

msgid "It's useful for marking noise words."
msgstr "Dit is nuttig om ruiswoorde te merk."

msgid ""
"A result that contains such a word will be rated lower than others, but will"
" not be excluded altogether, as it would be with the minus operator."
msgstr ""
"'n Resultaat wat so 'n woord bevat, sal laer gegradeer word as ander, maar "
"sal nie heeltemal uitgesluit word nie, soos met die minus-operateur."

msgid "An asterisk is the wildcard operator."
msgstr "'n Sterretjie is die jokerteken-operateur."

msgid ""
"Unlike the other operators, it is appended to the word, or fragment, not "
"prepended."
msgstr ""
"Anders as die ander operateurs, word dit aan die woord, of fragment, geheg, "
"nie voorgevoeg nie."

msgid ""
"This means that if there is a note with the word 'house', and you search for"
" '*ouse', this note will not be selected."
msgstr ""
"Dit beteken dat as daar 'n nota met die woord 'huis' is, en u soek na "
"'*uis', hierdie nota nie gekies sal word nie."

msgid "Yes, this is unusual, but this is how the database search works."
msgstr "Ja, dit is ongewoon, maar dit is hoe die databasissoektog werk."

msgid ""
"To minimize the pain of this, measures have been taken that if you type any "
"part of the word, the expected result will still be found."
msgstr ""
"Om die las hiervan te verminder, is maatreëls getref sodat as u enige deel "
"van die woord tik, die verwagte resultaat steeds gevind sal word."

msgid ""
"Double quotes at the beginning and end of a phrase, gives only the notes "
"that contain the complete phrase, as it was typed."
msgstr ""
"Dubbele aanhalingstekens aan die begin en einde van 'n frase gee slegs die "
"notas wat die volledige frase bevat, soos dit getik is."

msgid "Each note can be assigned to somebody."
msgstr "Elke nota kan aan iemand toegewys word."

msgid ""
"The person to whom the note is assigned then knows that action should be "
"taken on this note."
msgstr ""
"Die persoon aan wie die nota toegewys is, weet dan dat daar op hierdie nota "
"opgetree moet word."

msgid "Or the person can be automatically emailed if the note gets changed."
msgstr ""
"Of die persoon kan outomaties per e-pos in kennis gestel word as die nota "
"verander word."

msgid "The Consultation Notes can partly be operated by email."
msgstr "Die Konsultasienotas kan gedeeltelik per e-pos bedryf word."

msgid ""
"When you receive an email from Bibledit, and this email contains a "
"Consultation Note, then you can reply to this email."
msgstr ""
"Wanneer u 'n e-pos van Bibledit ontvang, en hierdie e-pos bevat 'n "
"Konsultasienota, kan u op hierdie e-pos antwoord."

msgid ""
"Your reply will be added as a comment to this particular Consultation Note."
msgstr ""
"U antwoord sal as 'n opmerking by hierdie spesifieke Konsultasienota gevoeg "
"word."

msgid ""
"The reply should come from the email address which you registered with "
"Bibledit when you created your  account."
msgstr ""
"Die antwoord moet kom van die e-posadres wat u by Bibledit geregistreer het "
"toe u u rekening geskep het."

msgid "The reply should also have (CSID123456789) in the subject line."
msgstr "Die antwoord moet ook (CSID123456789) in die onderwerpreël hê."

msgid "The number 123456789 is a Consultation Note Identifier."
msgstr "Die getal 123456789 is 'n Konsultasienota-identifiseerder."

msgid "It is different for every Note."
msgstr "Dit is verskillend vir elke Nota."

msgid ""
"Just replying to a Consultation Note you received is usually all that is "
"needed."
msgstr ""
"Om net op 'n Konsultasienota te antwoord wat u ontvang het, is gewoonlik al "
"wat nodig is."

msgid "Only replies that are typed before the quoted text are considered."
msgstr ""
"Slegs antwoorde wat voor die aangehaalde teks getik is, word in ag geneem."

msgid "This is called top-posting."
msgstr "Dit word top-posting genoem."

msgid ""
"When the quoted text gets posted too, then it is necessary to remove that "
"from your email reply."
msgstr ""
"Wanneer die aangehaalde teks ook gepos word, is dit nodig om dit uit u "
"e-posantwoord te verwyder."

msgid "You can also submit a new Consultation Note by email."
msgstr "U kan ook 'n nuwe Konsultasienota per e-pos indien."

msgid "This is how to do it:"
msgstr "Dit is hoe om dit te doen:"

msgid "Create a new email to the site's email address."
msgstr "Skep 'n nuwe e-pos aan die webwerf se e-posadres."

msgid ""
"The subject line contains 'New note', then the passage, and finally the "
"summary."
msgstr ""
"Die onderwerpreël bevat 'New note', dan die gedeelte, en laastens die "
"opsomming."

msgid "The body of the email will be the first comment on that note."
msgstr ""
"Die liggaam van die e-pos sal die eerste opmerking by daardie nota wees."

msgid "Lean Bible translation management"
msgstr "Skraal Bybelvertaalbestuur"

msgid "What is lean management?"
msgstr "Wat is skraal bestuur?"

msgid ""
"Lean management is about the systematic pursuit of desired translation "
"competence and conditions by utilizing human capabilities in a coordinated "
"manner."
msgstr ""
"Skraal bestuur gaan oor die stelselmatige strewe na gewenste "
"vertaalbevoegdheid en -toestande deur menslike vermoëns op 'n gekoördineerde"
" wyse te benut."

msgid "Two things are essential for this:"
msgstr "Twee dinge is hiervoor noodsaaklik:"

msgid "Developing desired conditions."
msgstr "Die ontwikkeling van gewenste toestande."

msgid "Developing capable people who can develop the desired conditions."
msgstr ""
"Die ontwikkeling van bekwame mense wat die gewenste toestande kan ontwikkel."

msgid "External reference"
msgstr "Eksterne verwysing"

msgid "Bibledit software"
msgstr "Bibledit-sagteware"

msgid "Copyright (©) 2003-2025 Teus Benschop."
msgstr "Kopiereg (©) 2003-2025 Teus Benschop."

