"This program is free software: you can redistribute it and/or modify it "
"under the terms of the GNU General Public License as published by the Free "
"Software Foundation, either version 3 of the License, or (at your option) "
"any later version."
msgstr ""
"Hierdie program is vrye sagteware: u kan dit herversprei en/of wysig onder "
"die bepalings van die GNU General Public License soos gepubliseer deur die "
"Free Software Foundation, óf weergawe 3 van die Lisensie, óf (na u keuse) "
"enige latere weergawe."

msgid ""
"This program is distributed in the hope that it will be useful, but without "
"any warranty; without even the implied warranty of merchantability or "
"fitness for a particular purpose. See the GNU General Public License for "
"more details."
msgstr ""
"Hierdie program word versprei in die hoop dat dit nuttig sal wees, maar "
"sonder enige waarborg; sonder selfs die geïmpliseerde waarborg van "
"verhandelbaarheid of geskiktheid vir 'n bepaalde doel. Sien die GNU General "
"Public License vir meer besonderhede."

msgid ""
"You should have received a copy of the GNU General Public License along with"
" this program. See also"
msgstr ""
"U behoort 'n kopie van die GNU General Public License saam met hierdie "
"program ontvang te het. Sien ook"

msgid "ETCBC4 Hebrew text database"
msgstr "ETCBC4 Hebreeuse teksdatabasis"

msgid ""
"The ETCBC database of the Hebrew Bible contains the scholarly text of the "
"Hebrew Bible with linguistic markup."
msgstr ""
"Die ETCBC-databasis van die Hebreeuse Bybel bevat die wetenskaplike teks van"
" die Hebreeuse Bybel met taalkundige merkers."

msgid "Original data source:"
msgstr "Oorspronklike databron:"

msgid "Bibledit's data source:"
msgstr "Bibledit se databron:"

msgid "SHEBANQ, a search engine for the Hebrew Bible"
msgstr "SHEBANQ, 'n soekenjin vir die Hebreeuse Bybel"

msgid "License:"
msgstr "Lisensie:"

msgid "Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial 4.0 International License"
msgstr "Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial 4.0 International License"

msgid "You may not use the data for commercial applications without consent."
msgstr ""
"U mag nie die data vir kommersiële toepassings gebruik sonder toestemming "
"nie."

msgid "Other code and data"
msgstr "Ander kode en data"

msgid ""
"All the code and data included in Bibledit that does not fall in the above "
"license categories has been licensed as mentioned in various bits of source "
"code included in Bibledit."
msgstr ""
"Al die kode en data wat by Bibledit ingesluit is en wat nie onder die "
"bogenoemde lisensiekategorieë val nie, is gelisensieer soos vermeld in "
"verskeie stukke bronkode wat by Bibledit ingesluit is."

msgid "See the source code repository."
msgstr "Sien die bronkode-bewaarplek."

msgid "Install Bibledit Cloud from a package"
msgstr "Installeer Bibledit Cloud vanaf 'n pakket"

msgid "Follow the steps below to install Bibledit Cloud."
msgstr "Volg die stappe hieronder om Bibledit Cloud te installeer."

msgid "Step"
msgstr "Stap"

msgid ""
"Install fixed version of Bibledit as it comes with the operating system."
msgstr ""
"Installeer vaste weergawe van Bibledit soos dit saam met die bedryfstelsel "
"kom."

msgid "Install most recent version of Bibledit."
msgstr "Installeer mees onlangse weergawe van Bibledit."

msgid "Install required software:"
msgstr "Installeer vereiste sagteware:"

msgid "Bibledit will be accessible through the IP address port 8080."
msgstr "Bibledit sal toeganklik wees deur die IP-adres poort 8080."

msgid "Examples:"
msgstr "Voorbeelde:"

msgid ""
"Open the web address in a browser, follow the instructions on the screen to "
"configure Bibledit Cloud, and log in."
msgstr ""
"Maak die webadres in 'n blaaier oop, volg die instruksies op die skerm om "
"Bibledit Cloud op te stel, en meld aan."

msgid "The following command shows the status of Bibledit Cloud:"
msgstr "Die volgende opdrag wys die status van Bibledit Cloud:"

msgid "Install Bibledit on Windows"
msgstr "Installeer Bibledit op Windows"

msgid "Bibledit runs on Windows 10 and 11."
msgstr "Bibledit loop op Windows 10 en 11."

msgid "Install Bibledit."
msgstr "Installeer Bibledit."

msgid "Start it through the menu."
msgstr "Begin dit deur die kieslys."

msgid "Give it enough time to download all the data from Bibledit Cloud."
msgstr "Gee dit genoeg tyd om al die data van Bibledit Cloud af te laai."

msgid "Bibledit is now ready for online and offline use."
msgstr "Bibledit is nou gereed vir aanlyn en vanlyn gebruik."

msgid ""
"There's a version for better performance and battery life on Windows on Arm."
msgstr ""
"Daar is 'n weergawe vir beter werkverrigting en batterylewe op Windows op "
"Arm."

msgid "Bibledit runs a number of checks on the text of the Bibles."
msgstr "Bibledit voer 'n aantal kontroles op die teks van die Bybels uit."

msgid "It does that every night."
msgstr "Dit doen dit elke nag."

msgid "Act on the results of the checks."
msgstr "Tree op volgens die resultate van die kontroles."

msgid "Receive the results by email."
msgstr "Ontvang die resultate per e-pos."

msgid "Notes."
msgstr "Notas."

msgid "You deal with checks on the Bibles you have write access to."
msgstr "U hanteer kontroles op die Bybels waartoe u skryftoegang het."

msgid "Install Bibledit iOS"
msgstr "Installeer Bibledit iOS"

msgid "Install Bibledit via the App Store."
msgstr "Installeer Bibledit via die App Store."

msgid "This works on an iPad or an iPhone running iOS 12 or higher."
msgstr "Dit werk op 'n iPad of 'n iPhone wat iOS 12 of hoër loop."

msgid "Hint."
msgstr "Wenk."

msgid "Switch off backup of Bibledit to iCloud via iOS."
msgstr "Skakel die rugsteun van Bibledit na iCloud via iOS af."

msgid "Bibledit Cloud already backs up Bibledit iOS."
msgstr "Bibledit Cloud maak reeds 'n rugsteun van Bibledit iOS."

msgid "If there were two backup mechanisms, that might  clash."
msgstr "As daar twee rugsteunmeganismes was, kan dit bots."

msgid "Read more."
msgstr "Lees meer."

msgid "Bibledit can host many Bibles."
msgstr "Bibledit kan baie Bybels huisves."

msgid "Many users can create an account."
msgstr "Baie gebruikers kan 'n rekening skep."

msgid ""
"A translation team is formed by giving a group of users access to a Bible."
msgstr ""
"'n Vertaalspan word gevorm deur 'n groep gebruikers toegang tot 'n Bybel te "
"gee."

msgid "A user may be granted read-only access to a Bible, or write access."
msgstr ""
"'n Gebruiker kan leestoegang tot 'n Bybel gegee word, of skryftoegang."

msgid "The type of access also depends on the role of a user."
msgstr "Die tipe toegang hang ook af van die rol van 'n gebruiker."

msgid "Manage users."
msgstr "Bestuur gebruikers."

msgid "Bibles can be made viewable by all users."
msgstr "Bybels kan deur alle gebruikers sigbaar gemaak word."

msgid "Manage Bibles."
msgstr "Bestuur Bybels."

msgid "Typesetting in Scribus 1.4 or higher"
msgstr "Setwerk in Scribus 1.4 of hoër"

msgid ""
"See the Scribus online help for more information and general principles."
msgstr "Sien die Scribus-aanlynhulp vir meer inligting en algemene beginsels."

msgid "Typesetting in Scribus starts with creating a new document."
msgstr "Setwerk in Scribus begin met die skep van 'n nuwe dokument."

msgid "Choose menu File / New."
msgstr "Kies kieslys Lêer / Nuut."

msgid "Document Layout: Double Sided."
msgstr "Dokumentuitleg: Dubbelsydig."

msgid "To make the grid visible, go to menu View / Show Baseline Grid."
msgstr ""
"Om die rooster sigbaar te maak, gaan na kieslys Bekyk / Wys basislynrooster."

msgid "Pick a Bible book, the version with text and note citations."
msgstr "Kies 'n Bybelboek, die weergawe met teks en nota-aanhalings."

msgid "Create a text frame in Scribus."
msgstr "Skep 'n tekskader in Scribus."

msgid "Add the text of the OpenDocument to this frame."
msgstr "Voeg die teks van die OpenDocument by hierdie kader."

msgid "I would like to place this extra text on a second page."
msgstr "Ek wil hierdie ekstra teks op 'n tweede bladsy plaas."

msgid "Create a new text frame on a new page."
msgstr "Skep 'n nuwe tekskader op 'n nuwe bladsy."

msgid "Link the new text frame with the previous text frame."
msgstr "Skakel die nuwe tekskader aan die vorige tekskader."

msgid ""
"There is still more text than fits on the second page. I estimate that there"
" is enough text to fill many pages."
msgstr ""
"Daar is nog steeds meer teks as wat op die tweede bladsy pas. Ek skat daar "
"is genoeg teks om baie bladsye te vul."

msgid "Place headlines"
msgstr "Plaas opskrifte"

msgid "The headline I have in this example is:"
msgstr "Die opskrif wat ek in hierdie voorbeeld het, is:"

msgid "'The first book of Moses called Genesis'."
msgstr "'Die eerste boek van Moses genaamd Genesis'."

msgid ""
"I'd like it to place it at the top of the page, and to span across any "
"columns."
msgstr ""
"Ek wil dit boaan die bladsy plaas, en dit oor enige kolomme laat strek."

msgid ""
"Select the relevant text frames, and drag the top to make it shorter, so "
"creating space above it."
msgstr ""
"Kies die relevante tekskaders, en sleep die bokant om dit korter te maak, en"
" sodoende ruimte daarbo te skep."

msgid "Create a new text frame at the top of the page."
msgstr "Skep 'n nuwe tekskader boaan die bladsy."

msgid "Estimate the size it needs to be."
msgstr "Skat die grootte wat dit moet wees."

msgid "Paste the text into that text frame."
msgstr "Plak die teks in daardie tekskader."

msgid "Resize the text frame so it looks smart."
msgstr "Verander die grootte van die tekskader sodat dit netjies lyk."

msgid ""
"Then resize the main text frame or frames so that everything looks good."
msgstr ""
"Verander dan die grootte van die hoofteksraam of -rame sodat alles goed lyk."

msgid "Make the setting to align it to the baseline grid."
msgstr "Maak die instelling om dit by die basislynrooster uit te lyn."

msgid "The leading of the text should be equal to the baseline grid."
msgstr ""
"Die reëlspasiëring van die teks moet gelyk wees aan die basislynrooster."

msgid ""
"If the leading of the text is bigger, then it is like as if you have double "
"line spacing."
msgstr ""
"As die reëlspasiëring van die teks groter is, is dit asof u dubbelspasiëring"
" het."

msgid "In this example, we expect an entire Bible to have about 1600 pages."
msgstr ""
"In hierdie voorbeeld verwag ons dat 'n hele Bybel ongeveer 1600 bladsye sal "
"hê."

msgid "Create a new document in Scribus."
msgstr "Skep 'n nuwe dokument in Scribus."

msgid "Take the file with all notes in OpenDocument format."
msgstr "Neem die lêer met alle notas in OpenDocument-formaat."

msgid "It is 00_Bible_notes.odt."
msgstr "Dit is 00_Bible_notes.odt."

msgid "Place the text as described above."
msgstr "Plaas die teks soos hierbo beskryf."

msgid ""
"Keep adding new text frames and linking them till all text has been placed."
msgstr ""
"Hou aan om nuwe tekskaders by te voeg en hulle te skakel totdat alle teks "
"geplaas is."

msgid "This allows us to see how many pages the notes will take up."
msgstr "Dit laat ons toe om te sien hoeveel bladsye die notas sal beslaan."

msgid "Place this text in the same way as above."
msgstr "Plaas hierdie teks op dieselfde manier as hierbo."

msgid "The font is of particular influence on the page count."
msgstr "Die lettertipe het besondere invloed op die bladsytelling."

msgid "This is not dealt with here."
msgstr "Dit word nie hier behandel nie."

msgid ""
"After exporting USFM text to OpenDocument, and properly placing this text "
"into Scribus, the USFM styles appear in Scribus."
msgstr ""
"Nadat USFM-teks na OpenDocument uitgevoer is, en hierdie teks behoorlik in "
"Scribus geplaas is, verskyn die USFM-style in Scribus."

msgid ""
"If you like to update a paragraph style, you may update each section heading"
" individually, but this is a lot of work."
msgstr ""
"As u 'n paragraafstyl wil opdateer, kan u elke afdelingsopskrif individueel "
"opdateer, maar dit is baie werk."

msgid ""
"It is faster to update the style for 's', so that this updates all "
"paragraphs that have this style."
msgstr ""
"Dit is vinniger om die styl vir 's' op te dateer, sodat dit alle paragrawe "
"wat hierdie styl het, opdateer."

msgid ""
"To update a paragraph style, place the cursor in it, and use the menu to "
"view or edit the style."
msgstr ""
"Om 'n paragraafstyl op te dateer, plaas die wyser daarin, en gebruik die "
"kieslys om die styl te bekyk of te wysig."

msgid "The Bible will have running headers."
msgstr "Die Bybel sal lopende opskrifte hê."

msgid "The headers contain the page number near the inside margin."
msgstr "Die opskrifte bevat die bladsynommer naby die binnekantlyn."

msgid "At the right margin it shows book and chapter numbers on that page."
msgstr ""
"By die regterkantlyn wys dit boek- en hoofstuknommers op daardie bladsy."

msgid "To do that, apply no master page to that particular page."
msgstr ""
"Om dit te doen, pas geen meesterbladsy op daardie spesifieke bladsy toe nie."

msgid "All that is needed is a fixed space after the chapter numbers."
msgstr "Al wat nodig is, is 'n vaste spasie na die hoofstuknommers."

msgid "Pick any one from a hair space to an em space."
msgstr "Kies enige een van 'n haarspasie tot 'n em-spasie."

msgid "The number of characters in drop caps is now increased by one."
msgstr "Die aantal karakters in sierletters word nou met een verhoog."

msgid "Set this value in the drop cap settings."
msgstr "Stel hierdie waarde in die sierletter-instellings."

msgid "All lines after the first will automatically line up."
msgstr "Alle reëls na die eerste sal outomaties belyn."

msgid ""
"Adjusting the spacing between words to produce tighter or looser paragraphs."
msgstr ""
"Pas die spasiëring tussen woorde aan om stywer of losser paragrawe te lewer."

msgid ""
"Adjusting the tracking of the text. This is the overall spacing of the "
"letters in a paragraph or on a line. With a good font in justified "
"paragraphs this can usually be adjusted by up to -25 or +15 without it "
"looking too out of place."
msgstr ""
"Pas die spoorspasiëring van die teks aan. Dit is die algehele spasiëring van"
" die letters in 'n paragraaf of op 'n reël. Met 'n goeie lettertipe in "
"uitgevulde paragrawe kan dit gewoonlik tot -25 of +15 aangepas word sonder "
"dat dit te misplaas lyk."

msgid "Adjusting the hyphenation of words within the paragraph."
msgstr "Pas die woordafbreking binne die paragraaf aan."

msgid "Forcing a word down onto the next line using a soft return."
msgstr "Dwing 'n woord na die volgende reël met 'n sagte terugkeer."

msgid "Tips and Tricks"
msgstr "Wenke en truuks"

msgid "Extensions and plugins"
msgstr "Uitbreidings en inproppe"

msgid "Browser extensions and plugins may interfere with Bibledit."
msgstr "Blaaieruitbreidings en inproppe kan met Bibledit inmeng."

msgid "There was a case that the USFM editor didn't load the text."
msgstr ""
"Daar was 'n geval waar die USFM-redigeerder nie die teks gelaai het nie."

msgid "Disabling an extension in Chrome resolved it."
msgstr "Die deaktivering van 'n uitbreiding in Chrome het dit opgelos."

msgid "Enable consultants to view the Bible in a workspace"
msgstr "Stel konsultante in staat om die Bybel in 'n werkruimte te bekyk"

msgid ""
"Just add the desired Bible to the Resources through the link organizer."
msgstr ""
"Voeg net die verlangde Bybel by die Hulpbronne deur die skakel-"
"organiseerder."

msgid "Then add the Resources to the workspace through URL resource/index."
msgstr "Voeg dan die Hulpbronne by die werkruimte deur URL resource/index."

msgid "Backup"
msgstr "Rugsteun"

msgid "Bibledit does not do any backups of its own."
msgstr "Bibledit maak nie self enige rugsteun nie."

msgid "Backup is very important."
msgstr "Rugsteun is baie belangrik."

msgid ""
"The system administrator should have a reliable backup strategy in place."
msgstr ""
"Die stelseladministrateur behoort 'n betroubare rugsteunstrategie in plek te"
" hê."

msgid "Bibledit uses SQLite for data storage."
msgstr "Bibledit gebruik SQLite vir databerging."

msgid ""
"If a database is backed up while SQLite is storing data in it, the database "
"may get malformed."
msgstr ""
"As 'n databasis gerugsteun word terwyl SQLite data daarin stoor, kan die "
"databasis beskadig raak."

msgid "Information."
msgstr "Inligting."

msgid "This applies to any database software, not just SQLite."
msgstr "Dit geld vir enige databasissagteware, nie net SQLite nie."

msgid ""
"To accommodate backup, Bibledit does not access databases from 0:00 to 0:05 "
"at midnight."
msgstr ""
"Om rugsteun te akkommodeer, kry Bibledit nie toegang tot databasisse van "
"0:00 tot 0:05 middernag nie."

msgid ""
"If no users access Bibledit during that time, then there is no database "
"access at all."
msgstr ""
"As geen gebruikers gedurende daardie tyd toegang tot Bibledit kry nie, is "
"daar glad nie databasistoegang nie."

msgid "Backup can be safely done during that time."
msgstr "Rugsteun kan veilig gedurende daardie tyd gedoen word."

msgid "If syncing no longer works, check the Journal for clues."
msgstr ""
"As sinchronisasie nie meer werk nie, kyk in die Joernaal vir leidrade."

msgid "The Journal may indicate any of the following:"
msgstr "Die Joernaal kan enige van die volgende aandui:"

msgid "This may be resolved in two ways:"
msgstr "Dit kan op twee maniere opgelos word:"

msgid ""
"Manually run the two commands in the appropriate directory from a terminal."
msgstr ""
"Voer die twee opdragte handmatig in die toepaslike gids vanaf 'n terminaal "
"uit."

msgid "Redo the setup of the Collaboration."
msgstr "Doen die opstelling van die Samewerking weer."

msgid "It will run those two commands for you."
msgstr "Dit sal daardie twee opdragte vir u uitvoer."

msgid "Bible books in custom order"
msgstr "Bybelboeke in pasgemaakte volgorde"

msgid "To sort the Bible books in a custom order, do this:"
msgstr "Om die Bybelboeke in 'n pasgemaakte volgorde te sorteer, doen dit:"

msgid "Go to menu Bible / Bibles."
msgstr "Gaan na kieslys Bybel / Bybels."

msgid "Select a Bible."
msgstr "Kies 'n Bybel."

msgid "Go to Book order."
msgstr "Gaan na Boekvolgorde."

msgid "Drag the books into the desired order."
msgstr "Sleep die boeke in die verlangde volgorde."

msgid "Font, text direction and writing mode of the Bible editors"
msgstr "Lettertipe, teksrigting en skryfmodus van die Bybelredigeerders"

msgid ""
"To set the font, the text direction, or the writing mode for the Bible text "
"editors, do this:"
msgstr ""
"Om die lettertipe, die teksrigting of die skryfmodus vir die "
"Bybelteksredigeerders te stel, doen dit:"

msgid "Go to Font and text direction."
msgstr "Gaan na Lettertipe en teksrigting."

msgid "Make the settings."
msgstr "Maak die instellings."

msgid "Restore a Bible from a git repository"
msgstr "Herstel 'n Bybel vanaf 'n git-bewaarplek"

msgid ""
"A Bible that has been backed up to a git repository, can also be restored "
"again from that repository."
msgstr ""
"'n Bybel wat na 'n git-bewaarplek gerugsteun is, kan ook weer vanaf daardie "
"bewaarplek herstel word."

msgid ""
"While linking this Bible to that repository afresh, take the Bible data from"
" that repository."
msgstr ""
"Terwyl hierdie Bybel opnuut aan daardie bewaarplek gekoppel word, neem die "
"Bybeldata van daardie bewaarplek."

msgid "That will restore the Bible."
msgstr "Dit sal die Bybel herstel."

msgid ""
"When there is a need to restore the Bible to an older commit in the "
"repository, copy the data from that older commit to the master branch, "
"commit it, then link this Bible afresh."
msgstr ""
"Wanneer daar 'n behoefte is om die Bybel na 'n ouer pleging in die "
"bewaarplek te herstel, kopieer die data van daardie ouer pleging na die "
"hooftak, pleeg dit, en koppel dan hierdie Bybel opnuut."

msgid ""
"When the Navigator is displayed, enter the passage to focus through the "
"keyboard."
msgstr ""
"Wanneer die Navigeerder vertoon word, voer die gedeelte om op te fokus deur "
"die sleutelbord in."

msgid "Escape"
msgstr "Escape"

msgid "Cancel any navigation or style operation."
msgstr "Kanselleer enige navigasie- of stylbewerking."

msgid "Alt-Down Arrow"
msgstr "Alt-Pyl af"

msgid "Navigate to the next verse."
msgstr "Navigeer na die volgende vers."

msgid "Alt-Up Arrow"
msgstr "Alt-Pyl op"

msgid "Navigate to the previous verse."
msgstr "Navigeer na die vorige vers."

msgid "Open the styles from the Bible editor."
msgstr "Maak die style vanaf die Bybelredigeerder oop."

msgid "Find text."
msgstr "Soek teks."

msgid "Find next."
msgstr "Soek volgende."

msgid "Print."
msgstr "Druk."

msgid "Cycle through the available Bible editors."
msgstr "Wissel deur die beskikbare Bybelredigeerders."

msgid "Scrum-based Translation"
msgstr "Scrum-gebaseerde vertaling"

msgid "What is Scrum-based translation?"
msgstr "Wat is Scrum-gebaseerde vertaling?"

msgid ""
"A translation team that works with Scrum frequently releases portions of "
"translated Scripture."
msgstr ""
"'n Vertaalspan wat met Scrum werk, stel gereeld dele van vertaalde Skrif "
"vry."

msgid ""
"This makes it clear to involved parties where the translation project is "
"going."
msgstr ""
"Dit maak dit vir betrokke partye duidelik waarheen die vertaalprojek op pad "
"is."

msgid ""
"It enables the translation team to make course corrections based on the "
"facts."
msgstr ""
"Dit stel die vertaalspan in staat om koerskorreksies op grond van die feite "
"te maak."

msgid ""
"Burndown charts and the product backlog provide the product owner and others"
" with a permanent overview over the translation status and progress."
msgstr ""
"Afbrandgrafieke en die produkagterstand gee die produkeienaar en ander 'n "
"permanente oorsig oor die vertaalstatus en -vordering."

msgid ""
"Scrum is an agile process that enables self-organizing translation teams to "
"deliver high translation output and accuracy in a short time."
msgstr ""
"Scrum is 'n ratse proses wat selforganiserende vertaalspanne in staat stel "
"om hoë vertaaluitset en akkuraatheid binne 'n kort tyd te lewer."

msgid ""
"Using iterative translation, it releases portions of translated Scripture "
"every iteration, say, every month."
msgstr ""
"Deur iteratiewe vertaling te gebruik, stel dit elke iterasie, sê maar elke "
"maand, dele van vertaalde Skrif vry."

msgid ""
"At the end of the every sprint, anyone can see the translated portion, and "
"decide whether to release it to the congregations and community for feedback"
" or continue to enhance it."
msgstr ""
"Aan die einde van elke sprint kan enigiemand die vertaalde gedeelte sien, en"
" besluit of dit aan die gemeentes en gemeenskap vir terugvoer vrygestel moet"
" word of verder verbeter moet word."

msgid ""
"The introduction and the following explanation just outlines the mechanics "
"of Scrum-based Translation."
msgstr ""
"Die inleiding en die volgende verduideliking skets slegs die meganika van "
"Scrum-gebaseerde Vertaling."

msgid ""
"It does not make clear what difficulties and issues you will run into trying"
" to implement it."
msgstr ""
"Dit maak nie duidelik watter probleme en kwessies u sal teëkom as u probeer "
"om dit te implementeer nie."

msgid "It only hints at the agile spirit that's required to make it work."
msgstr "Dit dui net die ratse gees aan wat nodig is om dit te laat werk."

msgid ""
"If you're interested in implementing Scrum-based translation, do some "
"reading, watch videos, follow a course, find a mentor or coach."
msgstr ""
"As u belangstel om Scrum-gebaseerde vertaling te implementeer, doen 'n "
"bietjie leeswerk, kyk video's, volg 'n kursus, vind 'n mentor of afrigter."

msgid "Product Owner"
msgstr "Produkeienaar"

msgid "The Product Owner represents the stakeholders."
msgstr "Die Produkeienaar verteenwoordig die belanghebbendes."

msgid ""
"He or she is the voice of the target audience, that is the Bible reader."
msgstr "Hy of sy is die stem van die teikengehoor, dit is die Bybellesers."

msgid "He understands the requirements for the Bible."
msgstr "Hy verstaan die vereistes vir die Bybel."

msgid "The Product Owner may also be a group of people in a committee."
msgstr "Die Produkeienaar kan ook 'n groep mense in 'n komitee wees."

msgid ""
"He is responsible for ensuring that the team delivers accuracy and "
"reliability to the Bible translation."
msgstr ""
"Hy is verantwoordelik om te verseker dat die span akkuraatheid en "
"betroubaarheid aan die Bybelvertaling lewer."

msgid "He knows about accuracy and reliability."
msgstr "Hy weet van akkuraatheid en betroubaarheid."

msgid "He defines items that focus on desired features."
msgstr "Hy definieer items wat op gewenste kenmerke fokus."

msgid ""
"He makes decisions as to whether to implement footnotes or leave them out."
msgstr ""
"Hy neem besluite oor of voetnotas geïmplementeer of weggelaat moet word."

msgid ""
"In the same way, he defines other features, like headers, introductions, or "
"decides to leave them out."
msgstr ""
"Op dieselfde manier definieer hy ander kenmerke, soos opskrifte, inleidings,"
" of besluit om dit weg te laat."

msgid "He decides about use or non-use of a dialect."
msgstr "Hy besluit oor die gebruik of nie-gebruik van 'n dialek."

msgid "He sets the priorities for the work to be done."
msgstr "Hy stel die prioriteite vir die werk wat gedoen moet word."

msgid "He adds the items to the product backlog."
msgstr "Hy voeg die items by die produkagterstand."

msgid "Scrum teams should have one Product Owner."
msgstr "Scrum-spanne moet een Produkeienaar hê."

msgid ""
"The Product Owner may be part of the Translation Team, but it is recommended"
" that his role not be combined with the role of Scrum Master."
msgstr ""
"Die Produkeienaar kan deel van die Vertaalspan wees, maar dit word aanbeveel"
" dat sy rol nie met die rol van Scrum-leier gekombineer word nie."

msgid "Release Planning"
msgstr "Vrystellingsbeplanning"

msgid ""
"The release planning shows which parts of the Bible will be translated and "
"delivered during which Sprint."
msgstr ""
"Die vrystellingsbeplanning wys watter dele van die Bybel gedurende watter "
"Sprint vertaal en gelewer sal word."

msgid ""
"It is convenient to define a Sprint in months, so that the release planning "
"mentions January, February, and so on."
msgstr ""
"Dit is gerieflik om 'n Sprint in maande te definieer, sodat die "
"vrystellingsbeplanning Januarie, Februarie, ensovoorts noem."

msgid ""
"It is often helpful to stick the release planning to the wall so that "
"everybody can see the grand picture."
msgstr ""
"Dit is dikwels nuttig om die vrystellingsbeplanning teen die muur te plak "
"sodat almal die groot prentjie kan sien."

msgid "The advantages of a release planning are:"
msgstr "Die voordele van 'n vrystellingsbeplanning is:"

msgid ""
"1. It gives the team a common vision about what needs to be achieved, and "
"when."
msgstr ""
"1. Dit gee die span 'n gemeenskaplike visie oor wat bereik moet word, en "
"wanneer."

msgid "2. It guides the team to make decisions during detailed planning."
msgstr ""
"2. Dit lei die span om besluite tydens gedetailleerde beplanning te neem."

msgid "3. It helps prioritize the actions."
msgstr "3. Dit help om die aksies te prioritiseer."

msgid ""
"4. It resolves conflicts and guides the teams toward the right balance on "
"trade-offs."
msgstr ""
"4. Dit los konflikte op en lei die spanne na die regte balans oor afwegings."

msgid ""
"Release each completed Bible book to the community and get their feedback."
msgstr ""
"Stel elke voltooide Bybelboek aan die gemeenskap vry en kry hul terugvoer."

msgid "This implements the important principle of continual improvement."
msgstr ""
"Dit implementeer die belangrike beginsel van voortdurende verbetering."

msgid "The release planning is a simple way of doing top-down planning."
msgstr ""
"Die vrystellingsbeplanning is 'n eenvoudige manier om bo-na-onder-beplanning"
" te doen."

msgid "It is an estimate, simple and quick to do."
msgstr "Dit is 'n skatting, eenvoudig en vinnig om te doen."

msgid "It is based on the Product Backlog."
msgstr "Dit is gebaseer op die Produkagterstand."

msgid "Product Backlog"
msgstr "Produkagterstand"

msgid ""
"The product backlog is an ordered list of requirements that is maintained "
"for the Bible translation."
msgstr ""
"Die produkagterstand is 'n geordende lys van vereistes wat vir die "
"Bybelvertaling gehandhaaf word."

msgid ""
"It consists of translation tasks, checking tasks, testing tasks, "
"comprehension tasks, whatever needs to be done to deliver a reliable "
"manuscript."
msgstr ""
"Dit bestaan uit vertaaltake, kontroletake, toetstake, begripstake, watter "
"ook al gedoen moet word om 'n betroubare manuskrip te lewer."

msgid "The Product Owner prioritizes the items on this list."
msgstr "Die Produkeienaar prioritiseer die items op hierdie lys."

msgid "It is used to determine the work for the next sprints."
msgstr "Dit word gebruik om die werk vir die volgende sprints te bepaal."

msgid "Each item has an associated estimated time to complete."
msgstr "Elke item het 'n gepaardgaande beraamde tyd om te voltooi."

msgid "A sprint typically takes one month."
msgstr "'n Sprint duur gewoonlik een maand."

msgid ""
"This is where the translaton work (translate, review, approve, test) occurs."
msgstr ""
"Dit is waar die vertaalwerk (vertaal, hersien, keur goed, toets) plaasvind."

msgid ""
"Each member of the team translates independently and in a responsible "
"manner."
msgstr ""
"Elke lid van die span vertaal onafhanklik en op 'n verantwoordelike manier."

msgid ""
"In case a translator is sure of a required change, he enters it without "
"consulting others."
msgstr ""
"In geval 'n vertaler seker is van 'n vereiste verandering, voer hy dit in "
"sonder om ander te raadpleeg."

msgid ""
"If a translator thinks a proposed change needs discussion, he notifies his "
"colleagues."
msgstr ""
"As 'n vertaler dink 'n voorgestelde verandering moet bespreek word, lig hy "
"sy kollegas in."

msgid ""
"All members of the translation team review the changes made by the team."
msgstr ""
"Alle lede van die vertaalspan hersien die veranderinge wat deur die span "
"gemaak is."

msgid ""
"This is to make sure that all changes are reviewed by all members, that no "
"mistakes occur."
msgstr ""
"Dit is om seker te maak dat alle veranderinge deur alle lede hersien word, "
"en dat geen foute voorkom nie."

msgid "The reviews take place every day."
msgstr "Die hersienings vind elke dag plaas."

msgid ""
"This way of working is based on personal responsibility and mutual trust."
msgstr ""
"Hierdie manier van werk is gebaseer op persoonlike verantwoordelikheid en "
"wedersydse vertroue."

msgid ""
"It speeds up the translation procedure because there's more actual "
"translation work going on, and less discussions."
msgstr ""
"Dit versnel die vertaalprosedure omdat daar meer werklike vertaalwerk aan "
"die gang is, en minder besprekings."

msgid ""
"The newer members of the team learn from the more experienced ones through "
"the daily reviews."
msgstr ""
"Die nuwer lede van die span leer deur die daaglikse hersienings van die meer"
" ervare lede."

msgid "Bibledit has the concept of daily Change Notifications."
msgstr "Bibledit het die konsep van daaglikse Veranderingskennisgewings."

msgid "A member can opt to receive the Change Notifications through email."
msgstr ""
"'n Lid kan kies om die Veranderingskennisgewings per e-pos te ontvang."

msgid "This email can be viewed online also."
msgstr "Hierdie e-pos kan ook aanlyn bekyk word."

msgid ""
"Or a member can opt to have the Change Notifications generated for him "
"online, and can review and approve them there."
msgstr ""
"Of 'n lid kan kies om die Veranderingskennisgewings aanlyn vir hom te laat "
"genereer, en kan dit daar hersien en goedkeur."

msgid "Sprint Planning Meeting"
msgstr "Sprintbeplanningsvergadering"

msgid ""
"During this meeting the team selects the portions to translate, review and "
"test it believes it can commit to in a sprint."
msgstr ""
"Tydens hierdie vergadering kies die span die gedeeltes om te vertaal, "
"hersien en toets waartoe hulle glo hulle in 'n sprint kan verbind."

msgid ""
"The team breaks the portions down into tasks and provided estimates for "
"those tasks as to the time it takes to complete them."
msgstr ""
"Die span breek die gedeeltes op in take en verskaf skattings vir daardie "
"take van die tyd wat dit neem om dit te voltooi."

msgid "Sprint Backlog"
msgstr "Sprintagterstand"

msgid "The sprint backlog is a list of tasks to be completed in a sprint."
msgstr ""
"Die sprintagterstand is 'n lys van take wat in 'n sprint voltooi moet word."

msgid ""
"The tasks are created by breaking down the product backlog items during the "
"planning meeting."
msgstr ""
"Die take word geskep deur die produkagterstanditems tydens die "
"beplanningsvergadering op te breek."

msgid "The tasks have estimates in hours or days associated with them."
msgstr "Die take het skattings in ure of dae daaraan gekoppel."

msgid ""
"For a team it is vitally important to have a clear goal to work towards."
msgstr ""
"Vir 'n span is dit uiters belangrik om 'n duidelike doel te hê om na toe te "
"werk."

msgid ""
"Thus everybody is focused on the desired outcome, and keeps a good pace."
msgstr "So is almal gefokus op die gewenste uitkoms, en hou 'n goeie tempo."

msgid ""
"Without a clear goal, the team may still do a lot of things and work hard, "
"but the produced results may not have the desired value."
msgstr ""
"Sonder 'n duidelike doel kan die span steeds baie dinge doen en hard werk, "
"maar die geproduseerde resultate het dalk nie die gewenste waarde nie."

msgid "Team"
msgstr "Span"

msgid ""
"The team consistes of the Bible translators, their assistants, and the "
"consultants."
msgstr ""
"Die span bestaan uit die Bybelvertalers, hul assistente en die konsultante."

msgid ""
"The team organizes itself to carry out the work and deliver a reliable and "
"good Bible translation."
msgstr ""
"Die span organiseer homself om die werk uit te voer en 'n betroubare en "
"goeie Bybelvertaling te lewer."

msgid "The team is quick but does not hurry."
msgstr "Die span is vinnig maar haas hom nie."

msgid "The team goes fast, but always has an eye on translation quality."
msgstr "Die span gaan vinnig, maar hou altyd die vertaalgehalte dop."

msgid "Scrum Master"
msgstr "Scrum-leier"

msgid "The scrum master organizes the translation process."
msgstr "Die scrum-leier organiseer die vertaalproses."

msgid "He or she keeps track of the progress of the translation team."
msgstr "Hy of sy hou die vordering van die vertaalspan dop."

msgid "He removes obstacles from the path of the team."
msgstr "Hy verwyder struikelblokke uit die span se pad."

msgid "Daily Scrum Meeting"
msgstr "Daaglikse Scrum-vergadering"

msgid ""
"On each day of a sprint, the Bible translation team holds daily meetings."
msgstr ""
"Op elke dag van 'n sprint hou die Bybelvertaalspan daaglikse vergaderings."

msgid "These meetings are called: Daily scrum meetings."
msgstr "Hierdie vergaderings word genoem: Daaglikse scrum-vergaderings."

msgid "The scrum meetings are held in the same place and at the same time."
msgstr ""
"Die scrum-vergaderings word op dieselfde plek en op dieselfde tyd gehou."

msgid "The meetings are typically held in front of Task Board."
msgstr "Die vergaderings word gewoonlik voor die Taakbord gehou."

msgid ""
"The daily scrum meeting is best held in the morning, because it assists in "
"setting the context for the work of that day."
msgstr ""
"Die daaglikse scrum-vergadering word die beste soggens gehou, omdat dit help"
" om die konteks vir die werk van daardie dag te stel."

msgid ""
"During the meeting, all members stand, as this keeps the discussion short "
"and relevant."
msgstr ""
"Gedurende die vergadering staan alle lede, aangesien dit die bespreking kort"
" en tersaaklik hou."

msgid "The scrum meeting is strictly time-boxed to 15 minutes."
msgstr "Die scrum-vergadering is streng tydgebonde tot 15 minute."

msgid ""
"There is a difference between people who are 'committed' to the Bible "
"translation project, and those who are 'involved' in it."
msgstr ""
"Daar is 'n verskil tussen mense wat tot die Bybelvertaalprojek 'toegewy' is,"
" en dié wat daarby 'betrokke' is."

msgid "Scrum affords special status to those who are committed."
msgstr "Scrum gee spesiale status aan dié wat toegewy is."

msgid ""
"Many teams enforce a rule in which only those who are committed are allowed "
"to talk during the daily scrum meeting."
msgstr ""
"Baie spanne handhaaf 'n reël waarvolgens slegs dié wat toegewy is, toegelaat"
" word om tydens die daaglikse scrum-vergadering te praat."

msgid "All team members are required to attend the scrum meetings."
msgstr "Alle spanlede word vereis om die scrum-vergaderings by te woon."

msgid ""
"The Scrum Master and the and Product Owner (usually the Bible Translation "
"Manager) are committed team members."
msgstr ""
"Die Scrum-leier en die Produkeienaar (gewoonlik die Bybelvertaalbestuurder) "
"is toegewyde spanlede."

msgid "They are expected to attend and participate."
msgstr "Daar word van hulle verwag om dit by te woon en daaraan deel te neem."

msgid ""
"Anyone else, for example a Church leader, a Committee member, or a "
"Translator from another team, is allowed to attend but is there to listen "
"only."
msgstr ""
"Enigiemand anders, byvoorbeeld 'n Kerkleier, 'n Komiteelid, of 'n Vertaler "
"van 'n ander span, mag bywoon, maar is daar net om te luister."

msgid ""
"This makes the daily scrum meeting an excellent way for a scrum team to "
"disseminate information."
msgstr ""
"Dit maak die daaglikse scrum-vergadering 'n uitstekende manier vir 'n scrum-"
"span om inligting te versprei."

msgid ""
"If you are interested in hearing the status of the project, attend that "
"day's meeting."
msgstr ""
"As u belangstel om die status van die projek te hoor, woon daardie dag se "
"vergadering by."

msgid ""
"The scrum meeting is not the place for solving problems or resolving issues."
msgstr ""
"Die scrum-vergadering is nie die plek om probleme of kwessies op te los nie."

msgid ""
"Issues that are raised are usually dealt with by one or two team members "
"immediately after the scrum."
msgstr ""
"Kwessies wat geopper word, word gewoonlik deur een of twee spanlede dadelik "
"na die scrum hanteer."

msgid ""
"During the daily Scrum, each team member answers the following three "
"questions:"
msgstr ""
"Gedurende die daaglikse Scrum beantwoord elke spanlid die volgende drie "
"vrae:"

msgid "What did you do yesterday?"
msgstr "Wat het u gister gedoen?"

msgid "What are you going to do today?"
msgstr "Wat gaan u vandag doen?"

msgid "Are there any impediments in your way?"
msgstr "Is daar enige struikelblokke in u pad?"

msgid ""
"The Scrum Master asks each team member to answer these questions, the member"
" speaks, the Scrum Master thanks the member, and then goes to the next "
"member."
msgstr ""
"Die Scrum-leier vra elke spanlid om hierdie vrae te beantwoord, die lid "
"praat, die Scrum-leier bedank die lid, en gaan dan na die volgende lid."

msgid ""
"By focusing on what each person did yesterday and will do today, the team "
"gains an understanding of what work has been done and what work remains."
msgstr ""
"Deur te fokus op wat elke persoon gister gedoen het en vandag gaan doen, "
"verkry die span 'n begrip van watter werk gedoen is en watter werk oorbly."

msgid ""
"The daily scrum meeting is not a status update meeting in which the boss is "
"finding out about who is slow in his work."
msgstr ""
"Die daaglikse scrum-vergadering is nie 'n statusopdateringsvergadering "
"waarin die baas uitvind wie stadig in sy werk is nie."

msgid ""
"Rather, it is a meeting in which team members make commitments to each "
"other."
msgstr ""
"Dit is eerder 'n vergadering waarin spanlede verbintenisse aan mekaar maak."

msgid ""
"If a translator says: Today, I will prepare chapter 10 and 11 of Matthew, "
"everyone knows that in tomorrow's meeting, he will say whether or not he did"
" finish."
msgstr ""
"As 'n vertaler sê: Vandag sal ek hoofstuk 10 en 11 van Matteus voorberei, "
"weet almal dat hy in more se vergadering sal sê of hy klaargemaak het of "
"nie."

msgid ""
"This has the wonderful effect of helping a team realize the significance of "
"these commitments, and that their commitments are to each other, and not to "
"anyone else."
msgstr ""
"Dit het die wonderlike effek om 'n span te help om die betekenis van hierdie"
" verbintenisse te besef, en dat hul verbintenisse aan mekaar is, en nie aan "
"enigiemand anders nie."

msgid ""
"Any impediments that are raised in the daily scrums become the Scrum "
"Master's responsibility to resolve as quickly as possible."
msgstr ""
"Enige struikelblokke wat in die daaglikse scrums geopper word, word die "
"Scrum-leier se verantwoordelikheid om so gou as moontlik op te los."

msgid "Typical impediments are:"
msgstr "Tipiese struikelblokke is:"

msgid "My ... broke and I need a new one today."
msgstr "My ... het gebreek en ek het vandag 'n nuwe een nodig."

msgid "I still haven't got the ... I requested a month ago."
msgstr "Ek het nog nie die ... gekry wat ek 'n maand gelede aangevra het nie."

msgid ""
"I'm struggling to understand ... and would like to discuss it with someone."
msgstr "Ek sukkel om ... te verstaan en wil dit met iemand bespreek."

msgid "The ... has asked me to work on something else for a few days."
msgstr "Die ... het my gevra om vir 'n paar dae aan iets anders te werk."

msgid ""
"In cases where the Scrum Master cannot remove these impediments directly "
"himself, he still takes responsibility for making sure someone on the team "
"does quickly resolve the issue."
msgstr ""
"In gevalle waar die Scrum-leier nie hierdie struikelblokke self direk kan "
"verwyder nie, neem hy steeds verantwoordelikheid om seker te maak dat iemand"
" in die span die kwessie wel gou oplos."

msgid "Every day a different person leads the daily scrum meeting."
msgstr "Elke dag lei 'n ander persoon die daaglikse scrum-vergadering."

msgid "This gets the entire team involved."
msgstr "Dit betrek die hele span."

msgid "It opens up new channels for communication."
msgstr "Dit maak nuwe kommunikasiekanale oop."

msgid "It builds trust between the Translators and the Scrum Master."
msgstr "Dit bou vertroue tussen die Vertalers en die Scrum-leier."

msgid "Team members can learn from one another's techniques."
msgstr "Spanlede kan van mekaar se tegnieke leer."

msgid ""
"The Scrum Master ensures to set a good example for leading the daily scrum "
"meeting."
msgstr ""
"Die Scrum-leier verseker dat hy 'n goeie voorbeeld stel vir die leiding van "
"die daaglikse scrum-vergadering."

msgid ""
"The scrum master uses the information from the meeting to update the "
"burndown chart illustrating progress."
msgstr ""
"Die scrum-leier gebruik die inligting uit die vergadering om die "
"afbrandgrafiek op te dateer wat vordering illustreer."

msgid "Side conversations are taken offline."
msgstr "Sygesprekke word vanlyn geneem."

msgid "Burn down chart"
msgstr "Afbrandgrafiek"

msgid ""
"A burn down chart is a graphical representation of work left to do versus "
"time."
msgstr ""
"'n Afbrandgrafiek is 'n grafiese voorstelling van werk wat nog gedoen moet "
"word teenoor tyd."

msgid "The outstanding work is on the vertical axis."
msgstr "Die uitstaande werk is op die vertikale as."

msgid "The days of the sprint are on the horizontal axis."
msgstr "Die dae van die sprint is op die horisontale as."

msgid "It is useful for predicting when all of the work will be completed."
msgstr "Dit is nuttig om te voorspel wanneer al die werk voltooi sal wees."

msgid "Sprint Review"
msgstr "Sprinthersiening"

msgid ""
"The Product Owner looks through the sprint’s work and provides feedback."
msgstr "Die Produkeienaar kyk deur die sprint se werk en gee terugvoer."

msgid "The Translators may demonstrate features."
msgstr "Die Vertalers kan kenmerke demonstreer."

msgid "The Team owns up to deficiencies with the translation."
msgstr "Die Span erken tekortkominge met die vertaling."

msgid "This attitude helps to build trust with the Product Owner."
msgstr "Hierdie houding help om vertroue met die Produkeienaar te bou."

msgid "Sprint Retrospective"
msgstr "Sprintterugblik"

msgid "The Team reviews what went well and what went poorly."
msgstr "Die Span hersien wat goed en wat swak gegaan het."

msgid "They use retrospection techniques to find potential for improvement."
msgstr ""
"Hulle gebruik terugblik-tegnieke om potensiaal vir verbetering te vind."

msgid "They pick one or two areas to focus for improvement."
msgstr "Hulle kies een of twee areas om op te fokus vir verbetering."

msgid "Typesetting Bibles"
msgstr "Setwerk van Bybels"

msgid "Bibledit can assist with typesetting."
msgstr "Bibledit kan met setwerk help."

msgid "But Bibledit is not designed for typesetting."
msgstr "Maar Bibledit is nie vir setwerk ontwerp nie."

msgid "It is for Bible editing."
msgstr "Dit is vir Bybelredigering."

msgid "No more than that."
msgstr "Nie meer as dit nie."

msgid "Having said this, and despite this, let's press on."
msgstr "Dit gesê, en ten spyte hiervan, kom ons gaan voort."

msgid "The Bible has been translated. It is time to publish it."
msgstr "Die Bybel is vertaal. Dit is tyd om dit te publiseer."

msgid "This article assists with typesetting the Bible."
msgstr "Hierdie artikel help met die setwerk van die Bybel."

msgid ""
"At the end of all, you will have a PDF file with part of the Bible, or the "
"whole Bible, typeset, ready for publishing."
msgstr ""
"Aan die einde van alles sal u 'n PDF-lêer hê met 'n deel van die Bybel, of "
"die hele Bybel, gesit, gereed vir publisering."

msgid "Basic assumptions"
msgstr "Basiese aannames"

msgid "The Bible is available in USFM code."
msgstr "Die Bybel is beskikbaar in USFM-kode."

msgid "The USFM code is clean and adheres to the standards."
msgstr "Die USFM-kode is skoon en voldoen aan die standaarde."

msgid "You have access to Bibledit."
msgstr "U het toegang tot Bibledit."

msgid "You have OpenOffice, LibreOffice or an equivalent."
msgstr "U het OpenOffice, LibreOffice of 'n ekwivalent."

msgid "Importing the USFM files"
msgstr "Voer die USFM-lêers in"

msgid ""
"This section describes the steps to take to prepare the USFM code for "
"export."
msgstr ""
"Hierdie afdeling beskryf die stappe om te volg om die USFM-kode vir uitvoer "
"voor te berei."

msgid "Each Bible book is stored as one USFM file."
msgstr "Elke Bybelboek word as een USFM-lêer gestoor."

msgid ""
"Create a new Bible in Bibledit. Give the Bible a name. The example calls it "
"'Ndebele'."
msgstr ""
"Skep 'n nuwe Bybel in Bibledit. Gee die Bybel 'n naam. Die voorbeeld noem "
"dit 'Ndebele'."

msgid "Click the 'Ndebele' Bible."
msgstr "Klik die 'Ndebele'-Bybel."

msgid "Import data into it."
msgstr "Voer data daarin in."

msgid "Choose the option to upload a file."
msgstr "Kies die opsie om 'n lêer op te laai."

msgid ""
"You can upload 66 separate files, or you can put all the 66 files into one "
"zipped file, and then upload that zipped file. Import takes a while. The "
"Journal shows the progress."
msgstr ""
"U kan 66 afsonderlike lêers oplaai, of u kan al 66 lêers in een gezipte lêer"
" plaas, en dan daardie gezipte lêer oplaai. Invoer neem 'n rukkie. Die "
"Joernaal wys die vordering."

msgid ""
"Create a new stylesheet in menu Styles. Give it a name. The example calls it"
" 'Ndebele'."
msgstr ""
"Skep 'n nuwe style-blad in kieslys Style. Gee dit 'n naam. Die voorbeeld "
"noem dit 'Ndebele'."

msgid ""
"All the data is now in Bibledit. Everthing is ready for export to "
"OpenDocument files."
msgstr ""
"Al die data is nou in Bibledit. Alles is gereed vir uitvoer na OpenDocument-"
"lêers."

msgid "The OpenDocument files are used as a starting point for typesetting."
msgstr "Die OpenDocument-lêers word as beginpunt vir setwerk gebruik."

msgid ""
"Some of the words in the OpenDocument files are long. This results in too "
"much space between some words."
msgstr ""
"Sommige van die woorde in die OpenDocument-lêers is lank. Dit lei tot te "
"veel spasie tussen sommige woorde."

msgid ""
"The words need to get hyphens so that part of the word goes on the next "
"line."
msgstr ""
"Die woorde moet koppeltekens kry sodat 'n deel van die woord op die volgende"
" reël kom."

msgid ""
"LibreOffice and Adobe InDesign and Scribus have hyphenation algorithms for "
"many languages. That would solve the problem."
msgstr ""
"LibreOffice en Adobe InDesign en Scribus het woordafbrekingsalgoritmes vir "
"baie tale. Dit sou die probleem oplos."

msgid "But the programs do not have hyphenation algorithms for all languages."
msgstr ""
"Maar die programme het nie woordafbrekingsalgoritmes vir alle tale nie."

msgid "Bibledit has a hyphenater that could assist."
msgstr "Bibledit het 'n woordafbreker wat kan help."

msgid "In Bibledit, go to this menu:"
msgstr "Gaan in Bibledit na hierdie kieslys:"

msgid "Enter the first set of characters, and the second set, and save it."
msgstr "Voer die eerste stel karakters in, en die tweede stel, en stoor dit."

msgid ""
"Set the Bible where to take the data from. In this case it is 'Ndebele'."
msgstr ""
"Stel die Bybel waarvan die data geneem moet word. In hierdie geval is dit "
"'Ndebele'."

msgid ""
"Insert the soft hyphens according to the setting. It takes a while to "
"complete."
msgstr ""
"Voeg die sagte koppeltekens in volgens die instelling. Dit neem 'n rukkie om"
" te voltooi."

msgid "The output Bible is called 'Ndebele-hyphenated'."
msgstr "Die uitvoer-Bybel word 'Ndebele-hyphenated' genoem."

msgid "Use this Bible from now on."
msgstr "Gebruik hierdie Bybel van nou af."

msgid "Exporting to OpenDocument files"
msgstr "Uitvoer na OpenDocument-lêers"

msgid "Make an initial export just to see how the text looks."
msgstr "Maak 'n aanvanklike uitvoer net om te sien hoe die teks lyk."

msgid "In Bibledit, go to menu Exports."
msgstr "Gaan in Bibledit na kieslys Uitvoere."

msgid "Add Bible 'Ndebele' to the ones that will be exported."
msgstr "Voeg Bybel 'Ndebele' by die een wat uitgevoer sal word."

msgid "Use stylesheet 'Ndebele'."
msgstr "Gebruik style-blad 'Ndebele'."

msgid "Output the chapter number in drop caps. Do not use frames."
msgstr "Lewer die hoofstuknommer in sierletters uit. Moenie rame gebruik nie."

msgid "Set the page size. I use this: width: 138 mm; height: 210 mm."
msgstr ""
"Stel die bladsygrootte. Ek gebruik hierdie: breedte: 138 mm; hoogte: 210 mm."

msgid ""
"Set the margins. I use this: 10 mm for top and bottom margins, 12 mm for the"
" outer margins, and 14 mm for the inner margins."
msgstr ""
"Stel die kantlyne. Ek gebruik hierdie: 10 mm vir boonste en onderste "
"kantlyne, 12 mm vir die buitekantlyne, en 14 mm vir die binnekantlyne."

msgid ""
"Do not display the date in the running headers. Switch that setting off."
msgstr ""
"Moenie die datum in die lopende opskrifte vertoon nie. Skakel daardie "
"instelling af."

msgid "Insert the 'en space' after verse numbers."
msgstr "Voeg die 'en-spasie' na versnommers in."

msgid "The Logbook shows the progress. Proceed when it is ready."
msgstr "Die Logboek wys die vordering. Gaan voort wanneer dit gereed is."

msgid ""
"Go to menu Exports and choose your Bible there. Then go to the OpenDocument "
"folder."
msgstr ""
"Gaan na kieslys Uitvoere en kies u Bybel daar. Gaan dan na die OpenDocument-"
"gids."

msgid "You will see the Bible exported into several formats."
msgstr "U sal die Bybel in verskeie formate uitgevoer sien."

msgid "Open the books in LibreOffice to see how they look."
msgstr "Maak die boeke in LibreOffice oop om te sien hoe hulle lyk."

msgid "The divine name will be underlined in the OpenDocument files."
msgstr "Die goddelike naam sal in die OpenDocument-lêers onderstreep wees."

msgid "The divine name is within this markup:"
msgstr "Die goddelike naam is binne hierdie merkers:"

msgid "Some prefer this in small capitals, not underlined."
msgstr "Sommige verkies dit in kleinhoofletters, nie onderstreep nie."

msgid "This can be changed in the stylesheet."
msgstr "Dit kan in die style-blad verander word."

msgid "Go to menu Styles, and choose the 'Ndebele' stylesheet."
msgstr "Gaan na kieslys Style, en kies die 'Ndebele'-style-blad."

msgid "Click the 'nd' style."
msgstr "Klik die 'nd'-styl."

msgid "Switch 'Underline' off."
msgstr "Skakel 'Onderstreep' af."

msgid "Switch 'Small caps' on."
msgstr "Skakel 'Kleinhoofletters' aan."

msgid ""
"Do a new export, wait a while, and review the OpenDocument files again."
msgstr ""
"Doen 'n nuwe uitvoer, wag 'n rukkie, en hersien die OpenDocument-lêers weer."

msgid ""
"The verse numbers are in superscript. The verse numbers are small and "
"difficult to read."
msgstr ""
"Die versnommers is in boskrif. Die versnommers is klein en moeilik om te "
"lees."

msgid "The intended audience prefers the verse numbers in bigger print."
msgstr "Die beoogde gehoor verkies die versnommers in groter druk."

msgid "Go to the relevant stylesheet and choose the 'v' style."
msgstr "Gaan na die relevante style-blad en kies die 'v'-styl."

msgid "Switch 'Superscript' off."
msgstr "Skakel 'Boskrif' af."

msgid "Do a new export and review the OpenDocument files."
msgstr "Doen 'n nuwe uitvoer en hersien die OpenDocument-lêers."

msgid ""
"The text in the OpenDocument files has been divided into paragraphs. New "
"paragraphs start when appropriate in the context. This is how the USFM files"
" have been marked up."
msgstr ""
"Die teks in die OpenDocument-lêers is in paragrawe verdeel. Nuwe paragrawe "
"begin wanneer toepaslik in die konteks. Dit is hoe die USFM-lêers gemerk is."

msgid ""
"The people who are going to read this Bible prefer each verse to start a new"
" paragraph."
msgstr ""
"Die mense wat hierdie Bybel gaan lees, verkies dat elke vers 'n nuwe "
"paragraaf begin."

msgid "Go to the stylesheet, and choose the 'v' style."
msgstr "Gaan na die style-blad, en kies die 'v'-styl."

msgid "Set 'Restart paragraph' on."
msgstr "Stel 'Herbegin paragraaf' aan."

msgid "Export again."
msgstr "Voer weer uit."

msgid ""
"Since each verse starts a new paragraph, there is no longer any need to "
"indent the first line of that paragraph."
msgstr ""
"Aangesien elke vers 'n nuwe paragraaf begin, is daar nie meer 'n behoefte om"
" die eerste reël van daardie paragraaf te laat inkeep nie."

msgid "In the stylesheet, edit the 'p' style."
msgstr "Wysig die 'p'-styl in die style-blad."

msgid "Set the 'First line indent' to 0 mm."
msgstr "Stel die 'Eerste reël-inkeping' op 0 mm."

msgid ""
"Some verses are short. Chapters that start with short verses no longer have "
"the chapter number in drop caps in LibreOffice."
msgstr ""
"Sommige verse is kort. Hoofstukke wat met kort verse begin, het nie meer die"
" hoofstuknommer in sierletters in LibreOffice nie."

msgid ""
"This is because this verse is all on one line, and thus there is no space "
"for drop caps, as these need two lines of text."
msgstr ""
"Dit is omdat hierdie vers alles op een reël is, en dus is daar geen ruimte "
"vir sierletters nie, aangesien dit twee reëls teks nodig het."

msgid ""
"Setting the text in two columns in LibreOffice solves the problem. The drop "
"caps are back."
msgstr ""
"Om die teks in LibreOffice in twee kolomme te stel, los die probleem op. Die"
" sierletters is terug."

msgid ""
"The letters of the Bible text are too big. This takes up a lot of space. The"
" Bible would get too many pages."
msgstr ""
"Die letters van die Bybelteks is te groot. Dit neem baie spasie in beslag. "
"Die Bybel sou te veel bladsye kry."

msgid ""
"Find out which styles start paragraphs. In the Ndebele Bible, these are the "
"styles p, s, nb, d."
msgstr ""
"Vind uit watter style paragrawe begin. In die Ndebele-Bybel is dit die style"
" p, s, nb, d."

msgid "Set these styles to have a font size of 10 points."
msgstr "Stel hierdie style om 'n lettergrootte van 10 punte te hê."

msgid "The letters of the notes and crossreferences are too big."
msgstr "Die letters van die notas en kruisverwysings is te groot."

msgid "Set the fontsize of the styles ft and xt to 6 points."
msgstr "Stel die lettergrootte van die style ft en xt op 6 punte."

msgid ""
"Parts of the footnotes are in bold or italics or both. You may prefer it all"
" in normal script."
msgstr ""
"Dele van die voetnotas is in vet of kursief of albei. U verkies dit dalk "
"alles in normale skrif."

msgid ""
"Update the relevant footnote styles and switch bold and italics off. The "
"styles are fk, fl, fq, fqa."
msgstr ""
"Dateer die relevante voetnootstyle op en skakel vet en kursief af. Die style"
" is fk, fl, fq, fqa."

msgid "Typesetting guidelines"
msgstr "Setwerkriglyne"

msgid ""
"The following needs consideration if the Bible includes more than one book."
msgstr "Die volgende moet oorweeg word as die Bybel meer as een boek insluit."

msgid ""
"Does the next book follow on the same page on which the previous book "
"finished, or do the books follow on from one another in a different way?"
msgstr ""
"Volg die volgende boek op dieselfde bladsy waarop die vorige boek geëindig "
"het, of volg die boeke op 'n ander manier op mekaar?"

msgid ""
"Whatever method is chosen, it needs to be applied consistently throughout "
"the Bible."
msgstr ""
"Watter metode ook al gekies word, dit moet deurgaans konsekwent in die hele "
"Bybel toegepas word."

msgid ""
"Line spacing should be consistent throughout and should be placed line on "
"line across all pages."
msgstr ""
"Reëlspasiëring moet deurgaans konsekwent wees en reël-vir-reël oor alle "
"bladsye geplaas word."

msgid ""
"It means that all lines should line up with each other all the way down the "
"page and across all pages."
msgstr ""
"Dit beteken dat alle reëls heeltemal met mekaar moet belyn regdeur die "
"bladsy en oor alle bladsye."

msgid ""
"Then when the Bible is printed, the printed text will be back to back and "
"not show through from one side of the page to the other."
msgstr ""
"Wanneer die Bybel dan gedruk word, sal die gedrukte teks rug-aan-rug wees en"
" nie van die een kant van die bladsy na die ander deurskyn nie."

msgid ""
"In the typesetting software, this can be implemented by setting up a grid in"
" the document, and then aligning all text to this grid."
msgstr ""
"In die setsagteware kan dit geïmplementeer word deur 'n rooster in die "
"dokument op te stel, en dan alle teks by hierdie rooster uit te lyn."

msgid "The space after the verse numbers would be the same and consistent."
msgstr "Die spasie na die versnommers sal dieselfde en konsekwent wees."

msgid ""
"Bibledit exports the text to OpenDocument format using 'en spaces' after "
"each verse."
msgstr ""
"Bibledit voer die teks na OpenDocument-formaat uit deur 'en-spasies' na elke"
" vers te gebruik."

msgid "This ensures a consistent width of the spaces after the verse numbers."
msgstr ""
"Dit verseker 'n konsekwente breedte van die spasies na die versnommers."

msgid ""
"The verse numbers should be set closer to the text that follows than to the "
"preceding text."
msgstr ""
"Die versnommers moet nader aan die teks wat volg as aan die voorafgaande "
"teks gestel word."

msgid "Many fonts have half spaces and hair spaces that can be used for this."
msgstr ""
"Baie lettertipes het halwe spasies en haarspasies wat hiervoor gebruik kan "
"word."

msgid "Or set the kerning to a specific amount for the verse numbers."
msgstr "Of stel die kerning op 'n spesifieke hoeveelheid vir die versnommers."

msgid "Superscript numerals could also be considered for verse numbers."
msgstr "Boskrifsyfers kan ook vir versnommers oorweeg word."

msgid ""
"They are less intrusive while at the same time just as readable and easily "
"found if they are not made too small."
msgstr ""
"Hulle is minder opdringerig terwyl hulle net so leesbaar en maklik vindbaar "
"is as hulle nie te klein gemaak word nie."

msgid "They should be larger than any note citations in the text."
msgstr "Hulle moet groter wees as enige nota-aanhalings in die teks."

msgid ""
"The size of the superscript would be between 70 and 80 percent of the size "
"of the main text."
msgstr ""
"Die grootte van die boskrif sal tussen 70 en 80 persent van die grootte van "
"die hoofteks wees."

msgid ""
"The alignment of the drop caps chapter numbers to the text beside it is to "
"be consistent."
msgstr ""
"Die belyning van die sierletter-hoofstuknommers met die teks daarnaas moet "
"konsekwent wees."

msgid "There should be some space between the numbers and the text."
msgstr "Daar moet 'n bietjie spasie tussen die nommers en die teks wees."

msgid ""
"Drop cap characters should not be too large and not rise too far above the "
"height of the other letters on the first line."
msgstr ""
"Sierlettertekens moet nie te groot wees nie en nie te ver bokant die hoogte "
"van die ander letters op die eerste reël uitsteek nie."

msgid "The top of the highest letters should reach to about the same height."
msgstr ""
"Die bokant van die hoogste letters moet tot ongeveer dieselfde hoogte reik."

msgid ""
"The drop cap characters in the body of the text should not be indented."
msgstr ""
"Die sierlettertekens in die liggaam van die teks moet nie ingekeep wees nie."

msgid ""
"The chapter divisions would also benefit from some more space between them "
"and the text of the preceding chapter."
msgstr ""
"Die hoofstukindelings sal ook baat by 'n bietjie meer spasie tussen hulle en"
" die teks van die voorafgaande hoofstuk."

msgid ""
"When there is no heading above a chapter, it may be visually better to start"
" the chapter number with a line space before it."
msgstr ""
"Wanneer daar geen opskrif bokant 'n hoofstuk is nie, kan dit visueel beter "
"wees om die hoofstuknommer met 'n reëlspasie daarvoor te begin."

msgid ""
"The amount of space given to the Bible book headings should not be too much."
msgstr ""
"Die hoeveelheid spasie wat aan die Bybelboekopskrifte gegee word, moet nie "
"te veel wees nie."

msgid "But they can do with some space above and below them."
msgstr "Maar hulle kan 'n bietjie spasie bo en onder hulle gebruik."

msgid ""
"Subheadings should not appear squashed amongst the rest of the text and "
"would benefit from some space."
msgstr ""
"Onderopskrifte moet nie saamgedruk tussen die res van die teks verskyn nie "
"en sal baat by 'n bietjie spasie."

msgid "Subheadings do not need to be set on the grid."
msgstr "Onderopskrifte hoef nie op die rooster gestel te word nie."

msgid "They are much better set a little closer to the text that follows."
msgstr "Hulle word baie beter 'n bietjie nader aan die teks wat volg gestel."

msgid ""
"Subheadings are an addition and not Scripture, so it is appropriate to put "
"these in italics."
msgstr ""
"Onderopskrifte is 'n toevoeging en nie Skrif nie, dus is dit gepas om dit in"
" kursief te plaas."

msgid ""
"The space between the text and footnotes should not be too tight neither "
"unnecessarily large."
msgstr ""
"Die spasie tussen die teks en voetnotas moet nie te styf wees nie, en ook "
"nie onnodig groot nie."

msgid ""
"Keep the gap between the references in the footer and the main block of text"
" as consistent as possible."
msgstr ""
"Hou die gaping tussen die verwysings in die voet en die hoofblok teks so "
"konsekwent as moontlik."

msgid ""
"The footnotes and crossreferences should not have a large variation in how "
"far they finish from the foot of the page."
msgstr ""
"Die voetnotas en kruisverwysings moet nie 'n groot variasie hê in hoe ver "
"hulle van die voet van die bladsy eindig nie."

msgid ""
"In the crossreferences it is pleasing to have the chapter and verse number "
"kept together with the book name, especially as the small font on long lines"
" gives scope for this."
msgstr ""
"In die kruisverwysings is dit aangenaam om die hoofstuk- en versnommer saam "
"met die boeknaam te hou, veral omdat die klein lettergrootte op lang reëls "
"ruimte hiervoor bied."

msgid ""
"The columns should start at the same height and should be balanced at the "
"ends."
msgstr ""
"Die kolomme moet op dieselfde hoogte begin en aan die einde gebalanseer "
"wees."

msgid "The gap between the columns should be between 4 and 5 mm."
msgstr "Die gaping tussen die kolomme moet tussen 4 en 5 mm wees."

msgid ""
"The centre line dividing the two columns should start about level or very "
"slightly above the top of the highest ascenders on the first line of text in"
" a column and finish about level with the bottom of the lowest descenders on"
" the bottom line."
msgstr ""
"Die middellyn wat die twee kolomme skei, moet ongeveer gelyk met of baie "
"effens bokant die bokant van die hoogste stygers op die eerste reël teks in "
"'n kolom begin en ongeveer gelyk met die onderkant van die laagste dalers op"
" die onderste reël eindig."

msgid "The centre line may also be omitted, as most modern Bibles do."
msgstr ""
"Die middellyn kan ook weggelaat word, soos die meeste moderne Bybels doen."

msgid "The pages looks cleaner then."
msgstr "Die bladsye lyk dan skoner."

msgid ""
"The Psalm headers need consistent spaces before and after and should be "
"positioned closer to the Psalm that follows than to the Psalm before."
msgstr ""
"Die Psalmopskrifte benodig konsekwente spasies voor en na en moet nader aan "
"die Psalm wat volg as aan die Psalm daarvoor geplaas word."

msgid "A 10 mm margin is okay for the top and bottom margins."
msgstr "'n Kantlyn van 10 mm is in orde vir die boonste en onderste kantlyne."

msgid "A 12 mm margin is good for the outer margin."
msgstr "'n Kantlyn van 12 mm is goed vir die buitekantlyn."

msgid "The inner margin needs slightly more, for example 14 mm."
msgstr "Die binnekantlyn benodig effens meer, byvoorbeeld 14 mm."

msgid ""
"For singable Psalms, readability would be helped by distinguishing the verse"
" numbers visually."
msgstr ""
"Vir singbare Psalms sal leesbaarheid gehelp word deur die versnommers "
"visueel te onderskei."

msgid ""
"It is helpful to distinguish the running head, perhaps by using a semi-bold "
"version of the same font."
msgstr ""
"Dit is nuttig om die lopende opskrif te onderskei, miskien deur 'n halfvet "
"weergawe van dieselfde lettertipe te gebruik."

msgid ""
"One way in which the number of pages in a volume could be reduced without "
"loss of readability would be to choose a font with slightly shorter "
"ascenders and descenders and then tighten the leading (line spacing) "
"slightly."
msgstr ""
"Een manier waarop die aantal bladsye in 'n band verminder kan word sonder "
"verlies aan leesbaarheid, sou wees om 'n lettertipe met effens korter "
"stygers en dalers te kies en dan die reëlspasiëring effens te verstyf."

msgid ""
"When producing PDF output, the text needs to be monochrome black, not black "
"consisting of three or four colours."
msgstr ""
"Wanneer PDF-uitvoer geproduseer word, moet die teks eenkleurig swart wees, "
"nie swart wat uit drie of vier kleure bestaan nie."

msgid ""
"The last line of a verse or paragraph should not appear on its own at the "
"top of a column."
msgstr ""
"Die laaste reël van 'n vers of paragraaf moet nie alleen bo-aan 'n kolom "
"verskyn nie."

msgid ""
"The typesetting software will have a setting for 'orphans' to control this."
msgstr ""
"Die setsagteware sal 'n instelling vir 'weeskinders' hê om dit te beheer."

msgid ""
"An elegant way of avoiding orphans is to increase or decrease the tracking "
"of the text."
msgstr ""
"'n Elegante manier om weeskinders te vermy, is om die spoorspasiëring van "
"die teks te vermeerder of te verminder."

msgid ""
"This is the overall spacing of the letters in a paragraph or on a line."
msgstr ""
"Dit is die algehele spasiëring van die letters in 'n paragraaf of op 'n "
"reël."

msgid "Avoid hyphenations in the headings."
msgstr "Vermy woordafbreking in die opskrifte."

msgid "It is helpful to remove all discretionary hyphens from the headings."
msgstr ""
"Dit is nuttig om alle diskresionêre koppeltekens uit die opskrifte te "
"verwyder."

msgid ""
"Many book titles consist of a main title and a subtitle, like 'The gospel of"
" Matthew'."
msgstr ""
"Baie boektitels bestaan uit 'n hooftitel en 'n subtitel, soos 'Die evangelie"
" van Matteus'."

msgid "'Matthew' is the main title, and the rest is the subtitle."
msgstr "'Matteus' is die hooftitel, en die res is die subtitel."

msgid "It is good if there is a clear contrast on size between these two."
msgstr ""
"Dit is goed as daar 'n duidelike kontras in grootte tussen hierdie twee is."

msgid ""
"Say 24 points bold for the main title, and 14 points regular for the "
"subtitle."
msgstr ""
"Sê 24 punte vet vir die hooftitel, en 14 punte gewoon vir die subtitel."

msgid ""
"The number of hyphens used in a row should be few for enhanced readability."
msgstr ""
"Die aantal woordafbrekings op 'n ry moet min wees vir verbeterde "
"leesbaarheid."

msgid ""
"The number of hyphens used in a row should not amount to more than three "
"consecutive hyphenated lines."
msgstr ""
"Die aantal woordafbrekings op 'n ry moet nie meer as drie opeenvolgende "
"afgebroke reëls beloop nie."

msgid ""
"At times a word that is now hyphenated can be forced down onto the next "
"line, and become a non-hyphenated word there, without opening up the gaps "
"between the words too much on the line where the word came from."
msgstr ""
"Soms kan 'n woord wat nou afgebreek is na die volgende reël gedwing word, en"
" daar 'n nie-afgebreekte woord word, sonder om die gapings tussen die woorde"
" op die reël waarvandaan die woord gekom het te veel oop te maak."

msgid ""
"Hyphenation should be set to the optimum result for the column width but "
"then it is usually necessary to go over every page and make corrections "
"manually."
msgstr ""
"Woordafbreking moet op die optimum resultaat vir die kolombreedte gestel "
"word, maar dan is dit gewoonlik nodig om elke bladsy deur te gaan en "
"korreksies handmatig te maak."

msgid ""
"The main page numbering should start at the first page of Genesis, or "
"Matthew in case of New Testaments."
msgstr ""
"Die hoofbladsynommering moet by die eerste bladsy van Genesis begin, of "
"Matteus in die geval van Nuwe Testamente."

msgid "To avoid what are sometimes referred to as 'rivers' in the text."
msgstr "Om te vermy wat soms na 'riviere' in die teks verwys word."

msgid ""
"This is where large spaces between words cause rivers of white space to be "
"seen running through the text."
msgstr ""
"Dit is waar groot spasies tussen woorde veroorsaak dat riviere van wit "
"spasie deur die teks sigbaar is."

msgid ""
"The use of hyphenation or tracking adjustments are tools that can be used to"
" minimise the problem."
msgstr ""
"Die gebruik van woordafbreking of spoorspasiëringsaanpassings is gereedskap "
"wat gebruik kan word om die probleem te minimaliseer."

msgid "But as always they need to be used with discretion."
msgstr "Maar soos altyd moet hulle met oordeel gebruik word."

msgid "As a general rule text will be justified on the left and the right."
msgstr "As 'n algemene reël sal teks links en regs uitgevul word."

msgid ""
"A word, part of a word, or very short line should not appear by itself at "
"the end of a paragraph."
msgstr ""
"'n Woord, deel van 'n woord, of baie kort reël moet nie alleen aan die einde"
" van 'n paragraaf verskyn nie."

msgid ""
"This results in less much white space between paragraphs or at the bottom of"
" a page."
msgstr "Dit lei tot minder wit spasie tussen paragrawe of onderaan 'n bladsy."

msgid ""
"The main page numbering starts at the first page of the text of the "
"Scripture."
msgstr ""
"Die hoofbladsynommering begin by die eerste bladsy van die teks van die "
"Skrif."

msgid ""
"This first page of Scripture starts on the recto for left to right reading "
"scripts."
msgstr ""
"Hierdie eerste bladsy van die Skrif begin op die recto vir links-na-regs-"
"leesskrifte."

msgid "The recto is the right side of a two page spread."
msgstr "Die recto is die regterkant van 'n tweebladsy-oopslag."

msgid "For right to left scripts it starts on the verso."
msgstr "Vir regs-na-links-skrifte begin dit op die verso."

msgid "This is the left side of a two page spread."
msgstr "Dit is die linkerkant van 'n tweebladsy-oopslag."

msgid ""
"Due to subheadings starting in a new column, there may be spaces at the foot"
" of pages."
msgstr ""
"Weens onderopskrifte wat in 'n nuwe kolom begin, kan daar spasies onderaan "
"bladsye wees."

msgid ""
"They can be filled by carefully adjusting tracking in one of the paragraphs."
msgstr ""
"Dit kan gevul word deur die spoorspasiëring in een van die paragrawe "
"versigtig aan te pas."

msgid "The paragraph would then take up an extra line to fill that space."
msgstr "Die paragraaf sal dan 'n ekstra reël inneem om daardie spasie te vul."

msgid ""
"It may not always be possible to fill gaps completely without creating "
"unsightly spacing within paragraphs."
msgstr ""
"Dit is dalk nie altyd moontlik om gapings heeltemal te vul sonder om lelike "
"spasiëring binne paragrawe te skep nie."

msgid "It needs to be handled with common sense."
msgstr "Dit moet met gesonde verstand hanteer word."

msgid "The typesetting"
msgstr "Die setwerk"

msgid "The typesetting can be done in LibreOffice."
msgstr "Die setwerk kan in LibreOffice gedoen word."

msgid "Or in Scribus."
msgstr "Of in Scribus."

msgid "This is free software."
msgstr "Dit is vrye sagteware."

msgid ""
"The organisation may want to use specialized typesetting software like Adobe"
" InDesign."
msgstr ""
"Die organisasie wil dalk gespesialiseerde setsagteware soos Adobe InDesign "
"gebruik."

msgid "Scrum-based translation process."
msgstr "Scrum-gebaseerde vertaalproses."

msgid "Transparent, fair, and argued discussions"
msgstr "Deursigtige, regverdige en beredeneerde besprekings"

msgid "Use of reliable Hebrew and Greek manuscripts."
msgstr "Gebruik van betroubare Hebreeuse en Griekse manuskripte."

msgid "Looking for and depending on the help of the Lord Jesus."
msgstr "Soek na en afhanklik wees van die hulp van die Here Jesus."

msgid "Use of modern tools and technology."
msgstr "Gebruik van moderne gereedskap en tegnologie."

msgid ""
"Goal: Deliver a reliable Bible translation within a reasonable time frame."
msgstr ""
"Doel: Lewer 'n betroubare Bybelvertaling binne 'n redelike tydraamwerk."

msgid "Lean management"
msgstr "Skraal bestuur"

msgid "Typesetting in LibreOffice"
msgstr "Setwerk in LibreOffice"

msgid ""
"See the online help about typesetting for more information about some "
"general principles."
msgstr ""
"Sien die aanlyn hulp oor setwerk vir meer inligting oor 'n paar algemene "
"beginsels."

msgid "You have access to a copy of LibreOffice."
msgstr "U het toegang tot 'n kopie van LibreOffice."

msgid "Page count"
msgstr "Bladsytelling"

msgid ""
"Download the file with notes. It was exported above. It is called "
"00_Bible_notes.odt."
msgstr ""
"Laai die lêer met notas af. Dit is hierbo uitgevoer. Dit word "
"00_Bible_notes.odt genoem."

msgid "Open the file in LibreOffice."
msgstr "Maak die lêer in LibreOffice oop."

msgid ""
"Let it repaginate. A good way of doing this is to press Ctrl-P as if going "
"to print the document. Then it will repaginate. Cancel the print dialog."
msgstr ""
"Laat dit herpagineer. 'n Goeie manier om dit te doen is om Ctrl-P te druk "
"asof u die dokument gaan druk. Dan sal dit herpagineer. Kanselleer die "
"drukdialoog."

msgid "It will now give the page count that the notes are likely to take up."
msgstr ""
"Dit sal nou die bladsytelling gee wat die notas waarskynlik sal inneem."

msgid "In our case, this is about 300 pages."
msgstr "In ons geval is dit ongeveer 300 bladsye."

msgid ""
"Each chapter has headings. These headings do not belong to the notes. Thus "
"the page count is too high."
msgstr ""
"Elke hoofstuk het opskrifte. Hierdie opskrifte behoort nie tot die notas "
"nie. Dus is die bladsytelling te hoog."

msgid ""
"Notice that the paragraph style for these headings is called 'Heading 1'."
msgstr ""
"Let op dat die paragraafstyl vir hierdie opskrifte 'Heading 1' genoem word."

msgid ""
"Hide the headings. This can be done like this. Right-click on a heading. "
"Choose 'Edit Paragraph Style'. A dialog comes up. Choose tab 'Font Effects'."
" Tick option 'Hidden'."
msgstr ""
"Versteek die opskrifte. Dit kan so gedoen word. Regsklik op 'n opskrif. Kies"
" 'Wysig paragraafstyl'. 'n Dialoog verskyn. Kies oortjie 'Lettertipe-"
"effekte'. Merk opsie 'Versteek'."

msgid ""
"Repaginate, and notice the page count. In our case it is down to about 125."
msgstr ""
"Herpagineer, en let op die bladsytelling. In ons geval is dit af tot "
"ongeveer 125."

msgid ""
"Download the OpenDocument file with text and note citations. It was exported"
" above. It is called 00_Bible_text_and_note_citations.odt."
msgstr ""
"Laai die OpenDocument-lêer met teks en nota-aanhalings af. Dit is hierbo "
"uitgevoer. Dit word 00_Bible_text_and_note_citations.odt genoem."

msgid "The document has only one column."
msgstr "Die dokument het net een kolom."

msgid "Repaginate and notice the page count. In our case this is 1750."
msgstr "Herpagineer en let op die bladsytelling. In ons geval is dit 1750."

msgid ""
"This is not accurate since it applies to a column count of one rather than "
"two."
msgstr ""
"Dit is nie akkuraat nie, aangesien dit van toepassing is op 'n kolomtelling "
"van een eerder as twee."

msgid "Set the whole document to have two columns."
msgstr "Stel die hele dokument om twee kolomme te hê."

msgid ""
"Go to menu Format / Page. Choose the Columns tab. Choose two columns. Set "
"the spacing to 0.2 cm. Set a thin separator line. Click Ok."
msgstr ""
"Gaan na kieslys Formateer / Bladsy. Kies die Kolomme-oortjie. Kies twee "
"kolomme. Stel die spasiëring op 0.2 cm. Stel 'n dun skeidingslyn. Klik OK."

msgid "Repaginate and notice the page count. It is down to 1520."
msgstr "Herpagineer en let op die bladsytelling. Dit is af tot 1520."

msgid "We are now able to estimate the page count for the entire Bible:"
msgstr "Ons kan nou die bladsytelling vir die hele Bybel skat:"

msgid ""
"Text body 1520 pages. Notes 125 pages. Singable Psalms 200 pages. Estimated "
"total is 1845 pages."
msgstr ""
"Teksliggaam 1520 bladsye. Notas 125 bladsye. Singbare Psalms 200 bladsye. "
"Geskatte totaal is 1845 bladsye."

msgid "Using LibreOffice for typesetting"
msgstr "Gebruik LibreOffice vir setwerk"

msgid ""
"Having used LibreOffice for typesetting for some time, my experience is that"
" the program is suitable for typesetting Bibles."
msgstr ""
"Nadat ek LibreOffice vir 'n geruime tyd vir setwerk gebruik het, is my "
"ervaring dat die program geskik is vir die setwerk van Bybels."

msgid ""
"I'd like to give some hints about how to do typographic work in LibreOffice."
msgstr ""
"Ek wil graag 'n paar wenke gee oor hoe om tipografiese werk in LibreOffice "
"te doen."

msgid ""
"To meet the requirement that line spacing be consistent throughout and be "
"placed line on line across all pages, do the following:"
msgstr ""
"Om aan die vereiste te voldoen dat reëlspasiëring konsekwent moet wees en "
"reël-vir-reël oor alle bladsye geplaas moet word, doen die volgende:"

msgid ""
"Go to menu Format / Page, and enable Register-true. Set the reference style "
"to 'Text Body'. Press OK."
msgstr ""
"Gaan na kieslys Formateer / Bladsy, en aktiveer Register-getrou. Stel die "
"verwysingstyl op 'Teksliggaam'. Druk OK."

msgid ""
"Select all the text, and go to menu Format / Paragraph, and activate "
"Register-true. Press OK."
msgstr ""
"Kies al die teks, en gaan na kieslys Formateer / Paragraaf, en aktiveer "
"Register-getrou. Druk OK."

msgid ""
"The line spacing specified by the paragraph style 'Text Body' is now used as"
" the reference line spacing for all paragraphs that have the register-true "
"feature enabled."
msgstr ""
"Die reëlspasiëring wat deur die paragraafstyl 'Teksliggaam' gespesifiseer "
"word, word nou as die verwysingsreëlspasiëring gebruik vir alle paragrawe "
"wat die register-getrou-funksie geaktiveer het."

msgid ""
"The line spacing in the document is going to be consistent. It will be equal"
" to the line spacing of the reference style 'Text Body', or a multiple of "
"it."
msgstr ""
"Die reëlspasiëring in die dokument gaan konsekwent wees. Dit sal gelyk wees "
"aan die reëlspasiëring van die verwysingstyl 'Teksliggaam', of 'n veelvoud "
"daarvan."

msgid "Changing the line spacing."
msgstr "Verander die reëlspasiëring."

msgid "Change the line spacing in paragraph style 'Text Body'."
msgstr "Verander die reëlspasiëring in paragraafstyl 'Teksliggaam'."

msgid "Press F11 to get the Styles and Formatting dialog."
msgstr "Druk F11 om die Style en Formatering-dialoog te kry."

msgid "Locate style 'Text Body'."
msgstr "Vind styl 'Teksliggaam'."

msgid "Right-click it with the mouse, and choose menu Modify."
msgstr "Regsklik daarop met die muis, en kies kieslys Wysig."

msgid "Go to tab Indents & Spacing."
msgstr "Gaan na oortjie Inkepings en Spasiëring."

msgid ""
"Adjust the spacing above the paragraph, the spacing below the paragrap, and "
"the line spacing. Press OK."
msgstr ""
"Pas die spasiëring bokant die paragraaf, die spasiëring onder die paragraaf,"
" en die reëlspasiëring aan. Druk OK."

msgid ""
"It may happen that some paragraphs in the text used to have a line spacing "
"equal to the line spacing of style 'Text Body', but now suddenly take up a "
"multiple of it. This may happen when you have tightened the line spacing a "
"bit."
msgstr ""
"Dit kan gebeur dat sommige paragrawe in die teks vroeër 'n reëlspasiëring "
"gelyk aan die reëlspasiëring van styl 'Teksliggaam' gehad het, maar nou "
"skielik 'n veelvoud daarvan inneem. Dit kan gebeur wanneer u die "
"reëlspasiëring 'n bietjie verstyf het."

msgid ""
"To resolve this, make the line spacing of those paragraphs smaller than the "
"line spacing of style 'Text body'."
msgstr ""
"Om dit op te los, maak die reëlspasiëring van daardie paragrawe kleiner as "
"die reëlspasiëring van styl 'Teksliggaam'."

msgid "Updating a paragraph style."
msgstr "Dateer 'n paragraafstyl op."

msgid ""
"After exporting USFM text to OpenDocument, the paragraph styles of the USFM "
"document appear in LibreOffice."
msgstr ""
"Nadat USFM-teks na OpenDocument uitgevoer is, verskyn die paragraafstyle van"
" die USFM-dokument in LibreOffice."

msgid ""
"To update a paragraph style, right-click the text of this paragraph, and "
"choose menu Edit Paragraph Style..., and make the desired settings."
msgstr ""
"Om 'n paragraafstyl op te dateer, regsklik die teks van hierdie paragraaf, "
"en kies kieslys Wysig paragraafstyl..., en maak die verlangde instellings."

msgid "Exporting to PDF."
msgstr "Voer uit na PDF."

msgid "See menu File / Export as PDF."
msgstr "Sien kieslys Lêer / Voer uit as PDF."

msgid "Hiding the soft hyphens and non-breaking spaces."
msgstr "Versteek die sagte koppeltekens en vaste spasies."

msgid ""
"The soft hyphens and the non-breaking spaces are visible as grey fields that"
" clutter the page. To hide them, do this:"
msgstr ""
"Die sagte koppeltekens en die vaste spasies is sigbaar as grys velde wat die"
" bladsy deurmekaar maak. Om hulle te versteek, doen dit:"

msgid "Go to menu Tools / Options."
msgstr "Gaan na kieslys Gereedskap / Opsies."

msgid "Go to LibreOffice Writer / Formatting Aids."
msgstr "Gaan na LibreOffice Writer / Formateringshulpmiddels."

msgid "Untick display of custom hyphens."
msgstr "Ontmerk vertoon van pasgemaakte koppeltekens."

msgid "Untick display of non-breaking spaces."
msgstr "Ontmerk vertoon van vaste spasies."

msgid "Install Bibledit on Android"
msgstr "Installeer Bibledit op Android"

msgid "Install Bibledit from Google Play."
msgstr "Installeer Bibledit vanaf Google Play."

msgid "Give it a while to initialize."
msgstr "Gee dit 'n rukkie om te inisialiseer."

msgid "Alternative installation options:"
msgstr "Alternatiewe installasie-opsies:"

msgid "Versions"
msgstr "Weergawes"

msgid ""
"There is a Bibledit version for Windows, for the Mac, for Android, for iOS, "
"and for Linux."
msgstr ""
"Daar is 'n Bibledit-weergawe vir Windows, vir die Mac, vir Android, vir iOS,"
" en vir Linux."

msgid "These are all client editions of Bibledit."
msgstr "Dit is almal kliënteweergawes van Bibledit."

msgid "There is also a server edition of Bibledit."
msgstr "Daar is ook 'n bedienerweergawe van Bibledit."

msgid "That is 'Bibledit Cloud'."
msgstr "Dit is 'Bibledit Cloud'."

msgid "It runs on the web."
msgstr "Dit loop op die web."

msgid ""
"Bibledit Cloud has more capabilities than the standard Bibledit editions."
msgstr "Bibledit Cloud het meer vermoëns as die standaard Bibledit-weergawes."

msgid ""
"The standard Bibledit editions connect to an instance of Bibledit Cloud for "
"collaboration, keeping the devices in sync, and for backup."
msgstr ""
"Die standaard Bibledit-weergawes koppel aan 'n instansie van Bibledit Cloud "
"vir samewerking, om die toestelle gesinchroniseer te hou, en vir rugsteun."

msgid ""
"All Bibledit editions, including Bibledit Cloud, enable Bible translation."
msgstr ""
"Alle Bibledit-weergawes, insluitend Bibledit Cloud, maak Bybelvertaling "
"moontlik."

msgid ""
"With a fast internet connection, it is usually easiest to translate straight"
" in Bibledit Cloud through the web browser."
msgstr ""
"Met 'n vinnige internetverbinding is dit gewoonlik die maklikste om reguit "
"in Bibledit Cloud deur die webblaaier te vertaal."

msgid ""
"When the internet connection is slow, or when it is off at times, it is "
"recommended to translate through one of the standard Bibledit versions."
msgstr ""
"Wanneer die internetverbinding stadig is, of wanneer dit soms af is, word "
"dit aanbeveel om deur een van die standaard Bibledit-weergawes te vertaal."

msgid ""
"The changes made in this way can be synchronized with Bibledit Cloud through"
" Send/receive."
msgstr ""
"Die veranderinge wat op hierdie manier gemaak is, kan deur Stuur/ontvang met"
" Bibledit Cloud gesinchroniseer word."

msgid "Bibledit on Windows"
msgstr "Bibledit op Windows"

msgid "Bibledit on Android"
msgstr "Bibledit op Android"

msgid "Bibledit on macOS"
msgstr "Bibledit op macOS"

msgid "Bibledit on Linux"
msgstr "Bibledit op Linux"

msgid "Bibledit on iOS"
msgstr "Bibledit op iOS"

msgid "Bibledit on Chrome OS"
msgstr "Bibledit op Chrome OS"

msgid "Bibledit Cloud on Linux"
msgstr "Bibledit Cloud op Linux"

msgid "Upgrading"
msgstr "Opgradering"

msgid ""
"A certain release of Bibledit can upgrade the most recent previous release, "
"but not older releases."
msgstr ""
"'n Sekere vrystelling van Bibledit kan die mees onlangse vorige vrystelling "
"opgradeer, maar nie ouer vrystellings nie."

msgid "A new release can be installed over the previous release."
msgstr "'n Nuwe vrystelling kan oor die vorige vrystelling geïnstalleer word."

msgid "There should be no loss of information."
msgstr "Daar behoort geen verlies van inligting te wees nie."

msgid ""
"Create a backup of the Bibledit folder before upgrading, just to be sure."
msgstr ""
"Skep 'n rugsteun van die Bibledit-gids voor opgradering, net om seker te "
"maak."

msgid "Clients"
msgstr "Kliënte"

msgid "The various Bibledit client editions store the data offline."
msgstr "Die verskillende Bibledit-kliënteweergawes stoor die data vanlyn."

msgid "You can translate the Bible on a client."
msgstr "U kan die Bybel op 'n kliënt vertaal."

msgid ""
"The user needs to regularly synchronize the data on the client with the data"
" on Bibledit Cloud."
msgstr ""
"Die gebruiker moet gereeld die data op die kliënt met die data op Bibledit "
"Cloud sinchroniseer."

msgid ""
"A Client is useful when the Internet connection to Bibledit Cloud is not "
"fast or not stable."
msgstr ""
"'n Kliënt is nuttig wanneer die Internetverbinding na Bibledit Cloud nie "
"vinnig of stabiel is nie."

msgid ""
"In the Bibledit client, connect to Bibledit Cloud once, and provide your "
"username and password as you normally log in on Bibledit Cloud."
msgstr ""
"Koppel in die Bibledit-kliënt een keer aan Bibledit Cloud, en verskaf u "
"gebruikersnaam en wagwoord soos u normaalweg by Bibledit Cloud aanmeld."

msgid "Also provide the port number."
msgstr "Verskaf ook die poortnommer."

msgid "Then synchronize the data."
msgstr "Sinchroniseer dan die data."

msgid ""
"The first time the client will download all Bible data and Notes from "
"Bibledit Cloud and store it offline."
msgstr ""
"Die eerste keer sal die kliënt alle Bybeldata en Notas van Bibledit Cloud "
"aflaai en vanlyn stoor."

msgid "That may take a while."
msgstr "Dit kan 'n rukkie neem."

msgid "After that, synchronizing will send and receive the changes only."
msgstr "Daarna sal sinchronisering slegs die veranderinge stuur en ontvang."

msgid ""
"The client mode is useful in a situation where the Internet connection is "
"not optimal."
msgstr ""
"Die kliëntmodus is nuttig in 'n situasie waar die Internetverbinding nie "
"optimaal is nie."

msgid "All data is stored locally on your computing device."
msgstr "Alle data word plaaslik op u rekenaartoestel gestoor."

msgid "During translation, the Internet connection is not used."
msgstr "Tydens vertaling word die Internetverbinding nie gebruik nie."

msgid "It is used during synchronization."
msgstr "Dit word tydens sinchronisering gebruik."

msgid "Bibledit Cloud works with email."
msgstr "Bibledit Cloud werk met e-pos."

msgid ""
"After completing the installation of Bibledit, sending and receiving emails "
"does not yet work."
msgstr ""
"Nadat die installasie van Bibledit voltooi is, werk die stuur en ontvang van"
" e-posse nog nie."

msgid "This needs to be set up."
msgstr "Dit moet opgestel word."

msgid ""
"Setting up the email means to pick an email address and setting details for "
"the mail servers in Bibledit."
msgstr ""
"Om die e-pos op te stel beteken om 'n e-posadres te kies en besonderhede vir"
" die poskedienerbedieners in Bibledit te stel."

msgid "This can be done from within the web application."
msgstr "Dit kan vanuit die webtoepassing gedoen word."

msgid "Multiple translation teams"
msgstr "Veelvuldige vertaalspanne"

msgid "There are two ways to have multiple translation teams on one server."
msgstr ""
"Daar is twee maniere om veelvuldige vertaalspanne op een bediener te hê."

msgid "Install multiple parallel copies of Bibledit on one server."
msgstr "Installeer verskeie parallelle kopieë van Bibledit op een bediener."

msgid ""
"Unpack the installation zip archive in sub folders with different names."
msgstr "Pak die installasie-zip-argief in subgidse met verskillende name uit."

msgid "Each copy has its own web address."
msgstr "Elke kopie het sy eie webadres."

msgid "Everything is completely separated between the parallel copies."
msgstr "Alles is heeltemal geskei tussen die parallelle kopieë."

msgid "This includes the data and the databases."
msgstr "Dit sluit die data en die databasisse in."

msgid "Every copy has its own independent databases."
msgstr "Elke kopie het sy eie onafhanklike databasisse."

msgid "Use one installation of Bibledit."
msgstr "Gebruik een installasie van Bibledit."

msgid "Give various users read or write access to various Bibles."
msgstr "Gee verskeie gebruikers lees- of skryftoegang tot verskeie Bybels."

msgid ""
"Users with write access together constitute a translation team that can edit"
" the Bible."
msgstr ""
"Gebruikers met skryftoegang vorm saam 'n vertaalspan wat die Bybel kan "
"redigeer."

msgid "Source code"
msgstr "Bronkode"

msgid "The Bibledit source code is kept in git repositories."
msgstr "Die Bibledit-bronkode word in git-bewaarplekke gehou."

msgid "Hosting"
msgstr "Gasheerdiens"

msgid "To run Bibledit Cloud, a Linux VPS (virtual private server) is needed."
msgstr ""
"Om Bibledit Cloud te laat loop, is 'n Linux-VPS (virtuele private bediener) "
"nodig."

msgid "Good providers are:"
msgstr "Goeie verskaffers is:"

msgid ""
"Several Bibledit users offer free assistance in setting up inexpensive "
"server hosting for Bibledit."
msgstr ""
"Verskeie Bibledit-gebruikers bied gratis hulp aan met die opstel van "
"goedkoop bedienergasheerdiens vir Bibledit."

msgid "If you would like this assistance, post a message to:"
msgstr "As u hierdie hulp wil hê, plaas 'n boodskap by:"

msgid "Security"
msgstr "Sekuriteit"

msgid ""
"There are various ways to improve the security of working with Bibledit."
msgstr ""
"Daar is verskeie maniere om die sekuriteit van werk met Bibledit te "
"verbeter."

msgid ""
"Securing traffic between a users' browsers and Bibledit Cloud, and between "
"Bibledit clients and Bibledit Cloud."
msgstr ""
"Beveilig verkeer tussen gebruikers se blaaiers en Bibledit Cloud, en tussen "
"Bibledit-kliënte en Bibledit Cloud."

msgid "Obfuscating Bibledit Cloud and Bibledit Linux clients."
msgstr "Verdoesel Bibledit Cloud en Bibledit Linux-kliënte."

msgid "Accessing Bibledit Cloud through a Tor browser."
msgstr "Toegang tot Bibledit Cloud deur 'n Tor-blaaier."

msgid "Configuration"
msgstr "Konfigurasie"

msgid "Here is more information about how to configure Bibledit Cloud."
msgstr "Hier is meer inligting oor hoe om Bibledit Cloud op te stel."

msgid "Install Bibledit on macOS"
msgstr "Installeer Bibledit op macOS"

msgid "This assumes a standard installation of the operating system."
msgstr "Dit veronderstel 'n standaard installasie van die bedryfstelsel."

msgid "Install Bibledit from the App Store."
msgstr "Installeer Bibledit vanaf die App Store."

msgid "Download Bibledit.zip from"
msgstr "Laai Bibledit.zip af vanaf"

msgid "Unpack it."
msgstr "Pak dit uit."

msgid "But most likely macOS will already have done this for you."
msgstr "Maar heel waarskynlik sal macOS dit reeds vir u gedoen het."

msgid "Drag Bibledit to the Applications folder."
msgstr "Sleep Bibledit na die Toepassings-gids."

msgid "Start it from the Applications."
msgstr "Begin dit vanaf die Toepassings."

msgid "Open Bibledit."
msgstr "Maak Bibledit oop."

msgid "Bibledit is ready for online and offline use."
msgstr "Bibledit is gereed vir aanlyn en vanlyn gebruik."

msgid ""
"Swiping right or left while displaying resources navigates to the previous "
"or next verse."
msgstr ""
"Om regs of links te swiep terwyl hulpbronne vertoon word, navigeer na die "
"vorige of volgende vers."

msgid "The same applies to the two verse-based Bible text editors."
msgstr "Dieselfde geld vir die twee versgebaseerde Bybelteksredigeerders."

msgid ""
"Swiping right or left in the two chapter-based Bible text editors navigates "
"to the previous of next chapter."
msgstr ""
"Om regs of links te swiep in die twee hoofstukgebaseerde "
"Bybelteksredigeerders, navigeer na die vorige of volgende hoofstuk."

msgid "Install Bibledit on Linux"
msgstr "Installeer Bibledit op Linux"

msgid "Supported Linux distributions:"
msgstr "Ondersteunde Linux-verspreidings:"

msgid "Install Bibledit on Ubuntu and derivatives."
msgstr "Installeer Bibledit op Ubuntu en afgeleides."

msgid "Other Linux distributions:"
msgstr "Ander Linux-verspreidings:"

msgid "Follow the steps below to install Bibledit"
msgstr "Volg die stappe hieronder om Bibledit te installeer"

msgid "Download the Bibledit Linux installer"
msgstr "Laai die Bibledit Linux-installeerder af"

msgid "Put it in the home directory."
msgstr "Plaas dit in die tuisgids."

msgid "Run the installer:"
msgstr "Voer die installeerder uit:"

msgid "Bibledit is an application for translating the Bible."
msgstr "Bibledit is 'n toepassing vir die vertaling van die Bybel."

msgid "People can sign up for an account and log in."
msgstr "Mense kan vir 'n rekening inskryf en aanmeld."

msgid "Each user has a certain role within the application."
msgstr "Elke gebruiker het 'n sekere rol binne die toepassing."

msgid ""
"The first role is Member. A member is somebody who has signed up to the "
"site, and has confirmed this signup through his email."
msgstr ""
"Die eerste rol is Lid. 'n Lid is iemand wat by die werf ingeskryf het, en "
"hierdie inskrywing deur sy e-pos bevestig het."

msgid ""
"The second role is Consultant. Consultants are people who can be consulted "
"because of their knowledge of the original language such as Hebrew or Greek,"
" or because of their knowledge of their target language in case they are "
"language scholars, or for any other knowledge they have."
msgstr ""
"Die tweede rol is Konsultant. Konsultante is mense wat geraadpleeg kan word "
"weens hul kennis van die oorspronklike taal soos Hebreeus of Grieks, of "
"weens hul kennis van hul teikentaal in geval hulle taalkundiges is, of vir "
"enige ander kennis wat hulle het."

msgid ""
"The next role is Translator. These are the ones that have all the rights of "
"the Consultant, but in addition can change the Bible text."
msgstr ""
"Die volgende rol is Vertaler. Dit is diegene wat al die regte van die "
"Konsultant het, maar bykomend die Bybelteks kan verander."

msgid ""
"Then there's the Manager. The manager has all the privileges of the previous"
" levels, but in addition can add books to the Bible, delete books, add "
"chapters, copy Bibles, and so on. The manager can assign privileges to the "
"translators, consultants, and so on."
msgstr ""
"Dan is daar die Bestuurder. Die bestuurder het al die voorregte van die "
"vorige vlakke, maar kan bykomend boeke by die Bybel voeg, boeke uitvee, "
"hoofstukke byvoeg, Bybels kopieer, ensovoorts. Die bestuurder kan voorregte "
"aan die vertalers, konsultante, ensovoorts toeken."

msgid ""
"Finally, there is the Administrator. The administrator has all rights to do "
"anything, and will do the technical setup and maintenance of the site."
msgstr ""
"Laastens is daar die Administrateur. Die administrateur het alle regte om "
"enigiets te doen, en sal die tegniese opstelling en instandhouding van die "
"werf doen."

msgid ""
"Everybody who has an account can enable the personal notifications. Those "
"who have switched the relevant notifications on can receive email from "
"Bibledit. They receive email when new consultation notes get created, or "
"when consultation notes get changed, or when consultation notes get assigned"
" to them. They can also get automatic daily email detailing the changes that"
" have been made in the Bible since the previous email."
msgstr ""
"Almal wat 'n rekening het, kan die persoonlike kennisgewings aktiveer. "
"Diegene wat die relevante kennisgewings aangeskakel het, kan e-pos van "
"Bibledit ontvang. Hulle ontvang e-pos wanneer nuwe konsultasienotas geskep "
"word, of wanneer konsultasienotas verander word, of wanneer konsultasienotas"
" aan hulle toegewys word. Hulle kan ook outomatiese daaglikse e-pos kry wat "
"die veranderinge uiteensit wat sedert die vorige e-pos in die Bybel gemaak "
"is."

msgid ""
"Everybody who has an account can create consultation notes by email, and "
"respond to these by email."
msgstr ""
"Almal wat 'n rekening het, kan konsultasienotas per e-pos skep, en daarop "
"per e-pos reageer."

msgid ""
"Members can view and download all exported Bibles and lists with recent "
"changes in the Bibles."
msgstr ""
"Lede kan alle uitgevoerde Bybels en lyste met onlangse veranderinge in die "
"Bybels bekyk en aflaai."

msgid ""
"Consultants can create consultation notes online, view these, set parameters"
" for these, assign the notes to people, and delete notes."
msgstr ""
"Konsultante kan konsultasienotas aanlyn skep, dit bekyk, parameters daarvoor"
" stel, die notas aan mense toewys, en notas uitvee."

msgid "Translators can do the following things:"
msgstr "Vertalers kan die volgende dinge doen:"

msgid "Edit the Bible text."
msgstr "Redigeer die Bybelteks."

msgid "Switch the stylesheet."
msgstr "Wissel die style-blad."

msgid "View and suppress results of the automatic checks."
msgstr "Bekyk en onderdruk resultate van die outomatiese kontroles."

msgid "Managers can do several things:"
msgstr "Bestuurders kan verskeie dinge doen:"

msgid "Edit the Bible in raw USFM format."
msgstr "Redigeer die Bybel in rou USFM-formaat."

msgid ""
"Send and receive the Bible text. This means that they can synchronize the "
"Bible text with a remote git repository. In this way they can collaborate "
"with people who use Bibledit-Gtk."
msgstr ""
"Stuur en ontvang die Bybelteks. Dit beteken dat hulle die Bybelteks met 'n "
"afgeleë git-bewaarplek kan sinchroniseer. Op hierdie manier kan hulle "
"saamwerk met mense wat Bibledit-Gtk gebruik."

msgid "View and clear the logbook."
msgstr "Bekyk en vee die logboek uit."

msgid "Process the changes, so that lists are created, and email is sent out."
msgstr ""
"Verwerk die veranderinge, sodat lyste geskep word, en e-pos uitgestuur word."

msgid "View and edit people who have an account, and create new accounts."
msgstr "Bekyk en wysig mense wat 'n rekening het, en skep nuwe rekeninge."

msgid "Create and delete Bibles, books, chapters, and import USFM data."
msgstr "Skep en vee Bybels, boeke, hoofstukke uit, en voer USFM-data in."

msgid ""
"Initiate the daily export of selected Bibles to OpenDocument, USFM, html, "
"Online Bible."
msgstr ""
"Begin die daaglikse uitvoer van geselekteerde Bybels na OpenDocument, USFM, "
"html, Online Bible."

msgid "Create and edit versification systems."
msgstr "Skep en wysig versifikasiestelsels."

msgid "Create and edit stylesheets."
msgstr "Skep en wysig style-blaaie."

msgid "Import consultation notes from Bibledit-Gtk and remove duplicates."
msgstr "Voer konsultasienotas van Bibledit-Gtk in en verwyder duplikate."

msgid "Deal with automatic hyphenation when exporting to OpenDocument."
msgstr "Hanteer outomatiese woordafbreking tydens uitvoer na OpenDocument."

msgid ""
"Make settings for the automatic check and select Bibles to run them on."
msgstr ""
"Maak instellings vir die outomatiese kontrole en kies Bybels om dit op uit "
"te voer."

msgid "Administrator can do several things:"
msgstr "Administrateur kan verskeie dinge doen:"

msgid "Set up Bibledit's email account."
msgstr "Stel Bibledit se e-posrekening op."

msgid ""
"Set up collaboration through setting up a connection with a remote git "
"repository."
msgstr ""
"Stel samewerking op deur 'n verbinding met 'n afgeleë git-bewaarplek op te "
"stel."

msgid "Maintain the databases."
msgstr "Onderhou die databasisse."

msgid "Set the site's timezone."
msgstr "Stel die werf se tydsone."

msgid "Set the site's language."
msgstr "Stel die werf se taal."

msgid "Install Bibledit Cloud from source"
msgstr "Installeer Bibledit Cloud vanaf bronkode"

msgid "Select the Linux distribution for which to show instructions."
msgstr "Kies die Linux-verspreiding waarvoor instruksies gewys moet word."

msgid "Then follow the steps below to install Bibledit Cloud."
msgstr "Volg dan die stappe hieronder om Bibledit Cloud te installeer."

msgid "Update the software sources."
msgstr "Dateer die sagtewarebronne op."

msgid "Install and enable extra package repositories."
msgstr "Installeer en aktiveer ekstra pakketbewaarplekke."

msgid "Install the software Bibledit relies on:"
msgstr "Installeer die sagteware waarop Bibledit staatmaak:"

msgid "Go to the home directory."
msgstr "Gaan na die tuisgids."

msgid "Download a recent version of Bibledit."
msgstr "Laai 'n onlangse weergawe van Bibledit af."

msgid "Unpack the downloaded Bibledit in folder bibledit."
msgstr "Pak die afgelaaide Bibledit in gids bibledit uit."

msgid ""
"Change the xxx above to the version number of Bibledit that was downloaded."
msgstr ""
"Verander die xxx hierbo na die weergawenommer van Bibledit wat afgelaai is."

msgid "Change to the directory."
msgstr "Verander na die gids."

msgid "Build Bibledit."
msgstr "Bou Bibledit."

msgid "This takes a while."
msgstr "Dit neem 'n rukkie."

msgid "There will be many technical messages, but there should be no errors."
msgstr ""
"Daar sal baie tegniese boodskappe wees, maar daar behoort geen foute te wees"
" nie."

msgid "Open port 8080 in the firewall."
msgstr "Maak poort 8080 in die brandmuur oop."

msgid "Start Bibledit."
msgstr "Begin Bibledit."

msgid "Most of Bibledit Cloud will now be working."
msgstr "Die meeste van Bibledit Cloud sal nou werk."

msgid ""
"To get email services working, connect Bibledit to a gmail or other mail "
"account."
msgstr ""
"Om e-posdienste aan die werk te kry, koppel Bibledit aan 'n gmail- of ander "
"posrekening."

msgid "To get SWORD resources working, install the SWORD libraries."
msgstr ""
"Om SWORD-hulpbronne aan die werk te kry, installeer die SWORD-biblioteke."

msgid ""
"Bibledit assists with checking how consistent words have been translated in "
"the Bible."
msgstr ""
"Bibledit help om na te gaan hoe konsekwent woorde in die Bybel vertaal is."

msgid "The suggested work-flow for consistency checking is this:"
msgstr "Die voorgestelde werkvloei vir konsekwentheidskontrole is dit:"

msgid ""
"Create a Consultation Note, and enter the details of the desired consistency"
" check, plus the passages to check."
msgstr ""
"Skep 'n Konsultasienota, en voer die besonderhede van die verlangde "
"konsekwentheidskontrole in, plus die gedeeltes om na te gaan."

msgid "Open the Consistency tool in a new tab."
msgstr "Maak die Konsekwentheidshulpmiddel in 'n nuwe oortjie oop."

msgid ""
"Copy the passages from the Consultation Note and paste them in the "
"Consistency tool."
msgstr ""
"Kopieer die gedeeltes uit die Konsultasienota en plak dit in die "
"Konsekwentheidshulpmiddel."

msgid "Enter the desired translation or translations in the Consistency tool."
msgstr ""
"Voer die verlangde vertaling of vertalings in die Konsekwentheidshulpmiddel "
"in."

msgid ""
"The Consistency tool will display the verse texts from the active Bible."
msgstr ""
"Die Konsekwentheidshulpmiddel sal die versteks uit die aktiewe Bybel "
"vertoon."

msgid "It will mark the translations in the verse."
msgstr "Dit sal die vertalings in die vers merk."

msgid "To make corrections, click a Passage."
msgstr "Om regstellings te maak, klik 'n Gedeelte."

msgid "The text editor will open at the correct chapter and verse."
msgstr "Die teksredigeerder sal by die korrekte hoofstuk en vers oopmaak."

msgid "Changes can be made in the text."
msgstr "Veranderinge kan in die teks gemaak word."

msgid "The Consistency tool will display any updates in the Bible."
msgstr ""
"Die Konsekwentheidshulpmiddel sal enige opdaterings in die Bybel vertoon."

msgid "The Consistency tool can display extra Bibles."
msgstr "Die Konsekwentheidshulpmiddel kan ekstra Bybels vertoon."

msgid "This assists the checking process."
msgstr "Dit help die kontroleproses."

msgid "Several pages have a Passage Navigator on top."
msgstr "Verskeie bladsye het 'n Gedeelte-navigeerder bo-aan."

msgid "It consists of the name of the book, the chapter, and the verse."
msgstr "Dit bestaan uit die naam van die boek, die hoofstuk en die vers."

msgid "Matthew 1:1."
msgstr "Matteus 1:1."

msgid "The navigator enables you to go to another passage."
msgstr "Die navigeerder stel u in staat om na 'n ander gedeelte te gaan."

msgid "Click on the name of the book to navigate to another book."
msgstr "Klik op die naam van die boek om na 'n ander boek te navigeer."

msgid "In the same way you can click on the chapter and on the verse."
msgstr "Op dieselfde manier kan u op die hoofstuk en op die vers klik."

msgid "You can also use the keyboard to navigate."
msgstr "U kan ook die sleutelbord gebruik om te navigeer."

msgid "On touch screens you can swipe to navigate."
msgstr "Op raakskerms kan u swiep om te navigeer."

msgid "The Navigator shows two arrows:"
msgstr "Die Navigeerder wys twee pyltjies:"

msgid "Clicking"
msgstr "Deur te klik"

msgid "goes back in the navigation history."
msgstr "gaan terug in die navigasiegeskiedenis."

msgid "goes forward in the navigation history."
msgstr "gaan vorentoe in die navigasiegeskiedenis."

msgid "There are also keyboard shortcuts for it."
msgstr "Daar is ook sleutelbordkortpaaie daarvoor."

msgid "A long click on any of these two arrows brings up the history menu."
msgstr ""
"'n Lang klik op enige van hierdie twee pyltjies bring die "
"geskiedenisskieslys op."

msgid "Some pages display one or more clickable passages."
msgstr "Sommige bladsye vertoon een of meer klikbare gedeeltes."

msgid "Clicking them updates the Passage Navigator."
msgstr "Deur daarop te klik word die Gedeelte-navigeerder opgedateer."

msgid "Username or email address:"
msgstr "Gebruikersnaam of e-posadres:"

msgid "Forgot password?"
msgstr "Wagwoord vergeet?"

msgid "Not registered?"
msgstr "Nie geregistreer nie?"

msgid "Sign up!"
msgstr "Skryf in!"

msgid "Signup"
msgstr "Inskrywing"

msgid "Your account is pending."
msgstr "U rekening is hangend."

msgid "A verification email has been sent."
msgstr "'n Verifikasie-e-pos is gestuur."

msgid "Follow the instructions in the email to activate your account."
msgstr "Volg die instruksies in die e-pos om u rekening te aktiveer."

msgid "Switched user"
msgstr "Gebruiker gewissel"

msgid "You have now logged in on behalf of another user:"
msgstr "U het nou namens 'n ander gebruiker aangemeld:"

msgid ""
"To go back to your own username, log this user out, and then login with your"
" own credentials."
msgstr ""
"Om terug te gaan na u eie gebruikersnaam, meld hierdie gebruiker af, en meld"
" dan aan met u eie magtigingsbewyse."

msgid "Which username would you like to use?"
msgstr "Watter gebruikersnaam wil u gebruik?"

msgid "Which password?"
msgstr "Watter wagwoord?"

msgid "Your email address?"
msgstr "U e-posadres?"

msgid "Security question:"
msgstr "Sekuriteitsvraag:"

msgid "Hint for answering the security question:"
msgstr "Wenk vir die beantwoording van die sekuriteitsvraag:"

msgid ""
"Submit your username or email address, and instructions will be emailed to "
"you."
msgstr ""
"Dien u gebruikersnaam of e-posadres in, en instruksies sal aan u per e-pos "
"gestuur word."

msgid "Identification"
msgstr "Identifikasie"

msgid ""
"File identification information (name of file, book name, language, last "
"edited, date, etc.)"
msgstr ""
"Lêeridentifikasie-inligting (naam van lêer, boeknaam, taal, laas geredigeer,"
" datum, ens.)"

msgid "USFM version"
msgstr "USFM-weergawe"

msgid ""
"USFM version specification for the file. Used to identify the USFM version "
"which a USFM editor / processor will be required to support in order to "
"manage all markup found within the file."
msgstr ""
"USFM-weergawespesifikasie vir die lêer. Gebruik om die USFM-weergawe te "
"identifiseer wat 'n USFM-redigeerder / -verwerker sal moet ondersteun om al "
"die merkers wat in die lêer gevind word, te bestuur."

msgid "Encoding"
msgstr "Enkodering"

msgid ""
"File encoding information. Bibledit disregards this marker, as all text in "
"Bibledit is in UTF-8 encoding."
msgstr ""
"Lêerenkoderingsinligting. Bibledit ignoreer hierdie merker, aangesien alle "
"teks in Bibledit in UTF-8-enkodering is."

msgid "Project text status tracking."
msgstr "Projekteksstatus-opsporing."

msgid "Remark"
msgstr "Opmerking"

msgid "Comments and remarks."
msgstr "Kommentaar en opmerkings."

msgid "Running header"
msgstr "Lopende opskrif"

msgid "Running header text for a book."
msgstr "Lopende opskrifteks vir 'n boek."

msgid "Left running header"
